1
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:19,620
<b><i>The walls granted the people one hundred years of peace.</i></b>

2
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:24,710
<b><i>The terror of being at their mercy</i></b>

3
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:29,940
<b><i>and the humiliation of being trapped in a 
birdcage became a distant memory for them.</i></b>

4
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,870
<b><i>However...</i></b>

5
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,980
<b><i>The battle for humanity's survival</i></b>

6
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,760
<b><i>began the moment the
Titans breached the wall.</i></b>

7
00:00:57,310 --> 00:01:04,820
<b><i>After innumerable casualties
among soldiers and civilians alike,</i></b>

8
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:09,900
<b><i>it was learned that some Titans
were hiding among the humans.</i></b>

9
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:16,490
<b><i>Finally, mankind succeeded in capturing 
one of these disguised Titans, Annie Leonhart,</i></b>

10
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:22,660
<b><i>in the fifth year since the breach of the wall.</i></b>

11
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:38,940
<b><i>The existence of the Wall Titan</i></b>

12
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:43,380
<b><i>had been kept secret by the Wall pastors</i></b>

13
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:46,740
<b><i>whereof one of them
was questioned by Hange ZoÃ«.</i></b>

14
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:51,780
<b><i>In the end, the pastor still kept quiet.</i></b>

15
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:01,080
So, Pastor Nick...

16
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:07,580
Are there Titans in <b><i>all</i></b> of the walls?

17
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,420
<b><i>However...</i></b>

18
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:14,020
<b><i>Humanity had no time to rest.</i></b>

19
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:18,090
<b><i>Since a new threat was already upon them.</i></b>

20
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,440
Faster! I need to get to Commander Erwin!

21
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,160
Faster!

22
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:31,070
Titans have appeared inside Wall Rose!

23
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:43,660
12 Hours Earlier

24
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:43,660
Wall Rose, Southern Region

25
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:48,600
Miche?

26
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,590
Tomas! Send out your fastest horses!

27
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:52,110
Four of them, you included!

28
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,850
I hear thuds! 
It sounds like footsteps!

29
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:58,890
What are you talking about, Sasha?

30
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:02,400
I'm telling the truth! 
I really did hear footâ€”

31
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,200
Nanaba...

32
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,870
Everyone present?

33
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:09,200
Multiple Titans are approaching from 500 meters south.

34
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:10,870
They're heading straight towards here.

35
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,220
There's no time for you to get equipped.

36
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,040
Get yourselves on horseback immediately,

37
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:18,160
alert the nearby civilians and villages, 
and evacuate the area.

38
00:03:18,650 --> 00:03:19,290
Got it?

39
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:21,780
From the south...

40
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,400
Does this mean the wall's been destroyed?

41
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,780
When the Titans get to the forest, everyone scatter at once!

42
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:34,110
We'll form four groups, starting now!

43
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:38,760
They'll be composed of the 104th's members and armed soldiers, one for each compass direction!

44
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:43,070
Avoid combat if at all possible and 
prioritize spreading the information!

45
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:45,690
Is anyone here familiar with the land?

46
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:47,310
Y-Yes, sir!

47
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,740
And Conny does, too!

48
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:52,650
My village is to the south...

49
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:55,220
...where the Titans are coming from.

50
00:03:56,050 --> 00:03:58,260
I can take you to the nearby villages.

51
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:01,960
After that, please let me go to my village.

52
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:03,960
All right.

53
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,040
You're in charge of guiding the south group.

54
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:07,960
Yes, sir.

55
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,910
The Titans have reached the forest!

56
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,380
Split up!

57
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,940
Ride as fast as you can!

58
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:31,510
Why did they all start running at once?

59
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:34,450
They're too fast! They'll catch up to us!

60
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:36,050
Gelgar!

61
00:04:36,050 --> 00:04:38,290
You're in charge of the south group!

62
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:39,180
Miche!

63
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,180
He can't do it alone! I'll go too!

64
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:44,580
No! We need manpower here!

65
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,580
Believe in Miche.

66
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:50,310
He's one of the Scout Regiment's 
best fighters, second only to Captain Levi!

67
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,270
Commander Pyxis!

68
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:18,820
Titans have appeared!

69
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:23,050
It appears that Wall Rose has been breached!

70
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:30,180
Good grief, would it kill 'em to give us a break?

71
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:34,420
Can you go?

72
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:36,250
What choice do I have?

73
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:40,490
Assigning Section Commander Miche as supervisor to the 104th was the right call.

74
00:05:40,490 --> 00:05:43,470
We just might be able to hold out.

75
00:05:43,470 --> 00:05:45,020
Yeah.

76
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:47,510
Let's hope so.

77
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:03,090
<b><i>Five down, four to go.</i></b>

78
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,220
<b><i>No, I should retreat while I can.</i></b>

79
00:06:07,470 --> 00:06:09,910
<b><i>I've bought them plenty of time.</i></b>

80
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:22,340
<b><i>But that Abnormal one bothers me.</i></b>

81
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,110
<b><i>It's huge.</i></b>

82
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:28,850
<b><i>I've never seen a Titan covered in a beast's pelt before.</i></b>

83
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,470
<b><i>Good! My horse is coming back!</i></b>

84
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:36,800
<b><i>Now I don't have to hold out until nightfall.</i></b>

85
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:45,890
<b><i>It went after the horse?</i></b>

86
00:06:46,290 --> 00:06:47,960
No! It can't be!

87
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:10,890
Wait.

88
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:36,850
Oh, come on, I told you to wait.

89
00:07:56,490 --> 00:08:00,020
What do you call that weapon of yours?

90
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:07,910
That thing on your hips, the thing you fly with.

91
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,910
Hmm... I thought we spoke the same language,

92
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:26,850
but I guess you're too scared to talk.

93
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:32,470
Oh, well. I'll just take it home.

94
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:57,760
<b><i>As long as we continue to fight...</i></b>

95
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:01,340
<b><i>...we are not defeated!</i></b>

96
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,600
Oh, you guys can move now!

97
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:31,450
So you <b><i>can</i></b> talk.

98
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:39,160
But still, they've come up with some really interesting things.

99
00:09:57,930 --> 00:10:06,400
<b>-  Roar of Awakening  -</b>

100
00:10:22,650 --> 00:10:24,620
Good grief, Eren.

101
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,510
Did you get in another fight?

102
00:10:27,510 --> 00:10:32,000
Those jerks started it! They made fun of me!

103
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:37,560
So, I assume Mikasa had to
come to your rescue again?

104
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:38,540
Thank you.

105
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:48,310
Eren, no matter how mean and hateful someone is,

106
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:50,760
that's no reason to start a fight.

107
00:10:52,290 --> 00:10:54,070
You're a man, aren't you?

108
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:57,580
You need to bear it and protect Mikasa.

109
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,690
That's...

110
00:11:46,690 --> 00:11:47,650
You dropped it.

111
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:51,690
You're tired. Go rest in your room.

112
00:11:51,690 --> 00:11:53,690
Sorry. I'm fine.

113
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,670
That thing's all worn out.

114
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:01,600
I'll get a new one for you if they come up in our provisions.

115
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,600
Eren! Mikasa!

116
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,400
This is really bad!

117
00:12:12,890 --> 00:12:15,860
There're Titans in Wall Rose!

118
00:12:16,010 --> 00:12:18,990
6 hours after the Titan sighting

119
00:12:16,010 --> 00:12:18,990
South Group

120
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:18,740
Conny, wait!

121
00:12:19,290 --> 00:12:20,740
Calm down!

122
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,160
There could be Titans anywhere!

123
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:25,020
Conny, fall back!

124
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,360
This can't be...

125
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:34,890
Anyone?! Is anyone there?!

126
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:37,870
It's me, Conny!

127
00:12:37,870 --> 00:12:40,760
I came back!

128
00:12:47,650 --> 00:12:49,580
My house!

129
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:52,690
<b><i>Dad...</i></b>

130
00:12:52,690 --> 00:12:54,340
<b><i>Mom...</i></b>

131
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:56,340
<b><i>Sunny... Martin...</i></b>

132
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,740
Please be okay!

133
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:14,000
Wel... com... ac...

134
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,690
Conny, get back!

135
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:23,690
Reiner, did you hear that?

136
00:13:23,690 --> 00:13:25,890
Just now, the Titan...

137
00:13:25,890 --> 00:13:29,340
It's crazy, but...

138
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:30,910
Everyone, stay back!

139
00:13:30,910 --> 00:13:32,910
Keep an eye on the surroundings!

140
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:36,160
Wait, it's...

141
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,160
It can't move?

142
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:41,160
Its limbs are too small.

143
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:49,450
7 hours after the Titan sighting

144
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:49,450
West Group

145
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,540
9 hours after the Titan sighting

146
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,540
Eastern Battlefront

147
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,960
9 hours after the Titan sighting

148
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,960
Trost District advance unit

149
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,460
This is strange...

150
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,250
We still haven't found the hole.

151
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,050
We haven't run into a single Titan yet, either.

152
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:12,360
Stohess District

153
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:16,760
What the hell is going on, anyway?

154
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,400
Damn...

155
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:22,820
Would Titans destroy a wall with Titans in it?

156
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:26,890
They've done it before. 
We lived in that very town.

157
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:29,310
No, that was the gate.

158
00:14:29,310 --> 00:14:32,090
Armin, what are you thinking about?

159
00:14:32,090 --> 00:14:35,540
The walls don't have joints between stones

160
00:14:35,540 --> 00:14:37,820
or traces of things being pulled off,

161
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:40,380
so I haven't been able to figure out how they were built,

162
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,870
but what if they used the Titans' hardening abilities?

163
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:49,670
Titans made the walls...?

164
00:14:56,310 --> 00:15:00,220
Wear it properly, Eren. It's cold at night.

165
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:02,220
Pardon the wait!

166
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:04,940
Sorry, it took me a while to get ready.

167
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:12,110
Um, what is a Wall pastor doing here?

168
00:15:12,470 --> 00:15:16,760
Oh, Nick and I are best buds! Ain't we?

169
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:18,760
Don't worry about him.

170
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:22,980
You know how we roll with info distribution in this squad.

171
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,980
Right, Levi?

172
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:26,710
No, there's a specific reason.

173
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:30,090
Erwin chose him.

174
00:15:30,850 --> 00:15:32,710
Gate opening!

175
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:43,470
We know nothing about the situation in Wall Rose,

176
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:46,580
so I can only guarantee our safety up until Ehrmich District!

177
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:48,800
We'll buy time there.

178
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:49,800
Let's move out!

179
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,270
Yes, sir!

180
00:15:51,710 --> 00:15:52,710
Move it.

181
00:15:52,710 --> 00:15:53,600
Yes, sir!

182
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:05,200
He <b><i>knew</i></b>?

183
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:09,580
This man <b><i>knew</i></b> there were Titans within the walls?!

184
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:14,160
Yeah, but he kept his mouth shut about it all this time.

185
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:19,780
We're gonna take him with us and show him the situation firsthand.

186
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:23,740
He said he wanted to see for himself

187
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:28,180
and then decide whether or not to talk.

188
00:16:28,180 --> 00:16:31,620
No way, that's just wrong!

189
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:34,460
If you know something, you have to say so!

190
00:16:34,810 --> 00:16:39,160
What could possibly be more important than preventing our extinction?

191
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,860
Eren, calm down.

192
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:43,690
You're still recovering from your transformation.

193
00:16:43,690 --> 00:16:46,060
There's more than one way to ask a question.

194
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:49,990
I may be too injured to fight right now,

195
00:16:49,990 --> 00:16:52,690
but I can at least keep an eye on our friend here.

196
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:59,240
Let's both be real careful, 
or someone will get a hole in them.

197
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:03,410
Threats don't work on him, Levi. I've already tried.

198
00:17:03,510 --> 00:17:08,910
The pastor comes off as a man of decent judgment to me.

199
00:17:08,910 --> 00:17:11,090
This is just my guess,

200
00:17:11,090 --> 00:17:13,390
but he might be keeping quiet for a reason

201
00:17:13,390 --> 00:17:17,660
that's worth risking humanity's extinction.

202
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:23,670
Ehrmich District

203
00:17:32,890 --> 00:17:37,140
Keep moving, pal. You're gonna get lost.

204
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:39,140
My word...

205
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:41,590
What did you expect to see?

206
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:45,160
This is what happens when the wall gets destroyed.

207
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:49,710
Mommy! Daddy!

208
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:56,390
Looks like someone was living here recently.

209
00:17:56,390 --> 00:17:58,460
Must've been some ne'er-do-wells' secret base.

210
00:17:59,690 --> 00:18:03,940
The sign said "Utgard Castle Ruins."

211
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:08,690
You, the south group, met us
after having followed the wall

212
00:18:08,690 --> 00:18:12,760
and couldn't find a hole anywhere.

213
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:17,410
Yeah. We'll have to check again tomorrow.

214
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,390
You newbies need to make sure you get nice and rested.

215
00:18:20,790 --> 00:18:23,640
I doubt there are any Titans that can still move now,

216
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,890
but the rest of us will keep watch on rotation, just in case.

217
00:18:25,890 --> 00:18:29,650
We set out four hours before sunrise.

218
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:30,990
Um...

219
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:34,310
If the wall really hasn't been destroyed,

220
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:38,160
then where did the Titans come from?

221
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:42,440
Well, um...

222
00:18:43,010 --> 00:18:46,610
Yeah, there doesn't seem to be too many Titans.

223
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:49,160
If the wall was destroyed, there would be more.

224
00:18:50,810 --> 00:18:55,110
Tomorrow, it'll be our job to figure that out.

225
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:05,560
Pastor Nick! Have you had a change of heart?

226
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:11,340
Can't you tell we're out of time?

227
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:14,590
Please, you need to hurry up and decide if you're gonna talk or not!

228
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:18,560
I cannot say anything.

229
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:23,310
My followers are of the same mind, and there is no swaying us.

230
00:19:23,310 --> 00:19:25,310
Oh, thank you so much!

231
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:28,690
Pardon me for wasting my time on you!

232
00:19:28,690 --> 00:19:34,260
It is far too great a decision to make on our own.

233
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:39,930
The Order of the Walls does 
naught but follows a great, unifying will.

234
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,180
Go ahead.

235
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:39,930
Thank you very much!

236
00:19:40,110 --> 00:19:41,930
Yeah? Whose?

237
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:43,290
Your God's?

238
00:19:43,290 --> 00:19:45,610
We cannot divulge that information.

239
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:46,760
However,

240
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:54,110
I can inform you of a name, who under the
sacred will, we were instructed to monitor.

241
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:55,310
Monitor?

242
00:19:56,310 --> 00:20:00,390
I have heard that this person 
joined the Scout Regiment this year.

243
00:20:03,490 --> 00:20:04,860
Her name is...

244
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:06,340
Urgent news!

245
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:09,890
104th Scout Regiment, 
Sasha Braus, reporting in!

246
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:13,040
Her?

247
00:20:13,390 --> 00:20:14,390
Who's that?

248
00:20:14,390 --> 00:20:17,190
Um, this is for you, Section Commander.

249
00:20:17,190 --> 00:20:19,660
You must find her at once.

250
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:25,010
She might know the truths which even we cannot perceive.

251
00:20:25,290 --> 00:20:28,310
That is all the information I can share.

252
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:32,210
The rest, I entrust to you.

253
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:36,560
But if she's in the 104th, then she's on the front lines...

254
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,790
Let's go! We need to hurry!

255
00:20:39,790 --> 00:20:41,090
Wait!

256
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:43,960
Sasha?

257
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,960
What are you doing here?

258
00:20:48,310 --> 00:20:51,640
When I went to make a report at a Regiment branch,

259
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:55,170
the higher-ups entrusted me with a document addressed to you!

260
00:20:55,610 --> 00:20:59,990
A document? Okay, thanks. Good work.

261
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:04,790
So anyway, who's that 104th girl?

262
00:21:04,790 --> 00:21:07,240
She's the shortest one.

263
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:12,210
She's got long, blonde hair, and, uh...

264
00:21:12,210 --> 00:21:13,660
She's cute.

265
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:15,840
She's the one who always hangs out with Ymir.

266
00:21:17,290 --> 00:21:18,640
Ymir?

267
00:21:25,340 --> 00:21:27,610
Ymir, what are you up to?

268
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:31,060
Oh, hey, Reiner. Looking for action, or something?

269
00:21:31,710 --> 00:21:36,290
I'm just looking for something to fill my stomach.

270
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:39,140
After all, it'll probably be my last supper.

271
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,810
Ooh, this looks promising.

272
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:43,990
Not really a fan of herring, butâ€”

273
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:47,040
Is there more? Lemme see.

274
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:50,440
Here.

275
00:21:50,910 --> 00:21:52,210
Canned food, huh?

276
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:59,790
What language is this? I can't read it at all.

277
00:22:00,990 --> 00:22:03,540
This says "herring"?

278
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:09,390
I'm surprised you could read this.

279
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:15,660
Ymir, are you...

280
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:17,310
Everyone, get up!

281
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:20,060
Come to the roof! Now!

282
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:26,910
The moon came out, and before I knew it...

283
00:22:26,910 --> 00:22:30,490
Why? Why can they move?

284
00:22:30,490 --> 00:22:32,740
It's been so long since the sun set!

285
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:34,860
What's happening?

286
00:22:34,860 --> 00:22:36,960
Hey, look at that!

287
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:40,760
It's huge. Is it even a Titan?

288
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:44,640
Like, it looks like a beast!

289
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:45,840
Right?

290
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:53,410
It's heading for the wall?

291
00:23:11,410 --> 00:23:13,940
Stay back, newbies!

292
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:18,740
This is a job for omni-directional mobility gear.

293
00:23:20,010 --> 00:23:21,360
Let's do this!

294
00:23:24,190 --> 00:23:26,090
Get your damn hands away from me!

295
00:23:26,090 --> 00:23:28,090
You piece of shit!

296
00:23:39,490 --> 00:23:41,010
Dumb idiot!

297
00:23:41,010 --> 00:23:42,790
That was dangerous!

298
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:46,690
Couldn't you have avoided that
without wasting your blades?

299
00:23:47,790 --> 00:23:50,060
The door's been broken!

300
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,440
A Titan's gotten in.

301
00:23:52,990 --> 00:23:55,990
Go back down and form some sort of barricade.

302
00:23:55,990 --> 00:23:57,840
You all have to do what you're trained.

303
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:59,840
Do everything you can while you're still alive!

304
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:00,840
Got it?

305
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,840
Roger!

306
00:24:04,660 --> 00:24:07,390
I'll go see how far the Titan's come!

307
00:24:07,390 --> 00:24:09,610
You guys grab boards or rods or whatever!

308
00:24:09,610 --> 00:24:11,610
Grab whatever you can!

309
00:24:11,610 --> 00:24:12,510
Reiner!

310
00:24:12,510 --> 00:24:14,040
Hey!

311
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:16,640
Wait, Reiner! Wait up!

312
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:20,540
He always runs ahead and takes the most dangerous jobs...

313
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:21,590
That maniac!

314
00:24:21,590 --> 00:24:24,260
Yeah, it's a bad habit of his.

315
00:24:30,690 --> 00:24:32,660
<b><i>Is it farther down?</i></b>

316
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:52,810
Down here!

317
00:24:53,210 --> 00:24:55,190
Bring me something, quick!

318
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:15,140
Reiner!

319
00:25:21,210 --> 00:25:22,960
You okay, Reiner?

320
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:27,640
Bertholdt, we're gonna survive and go home!

321
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:29,890
We're going back to our hometown for sure!

322
00:25:29,890 --> 00:25:32,340
Right... Right!

323
00:25:32,340 --> 00:25:34,060
Let's go home!

324
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:36,060
Reiner! Bertholdt!

325
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:37,710
Get out of the way!

326
00:25:50,110 --> 00:25:53,240
Looks like it worked out well, somehow.

327
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:55,410
What now? Should I cut off its nape?

328
00:25:55,410 --> 00:25:56,940
Don't even try.

329
00:25:56,940 --> 00:25:58,910
If it grabs you, you'll be in trouble.

330
00:25:58,910 --> 00:26:02,710
F-For now, let's retreat back upstairs.

331
00:26:02,710 --> 00:26:05,910
There could be more
than just one that got inside.

332
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:07,660
Conny!

333
00:26:15,610 --> 00:26:16,240
Reiner!

334
00:26:29,210 --> 00:26:30,690
Uh, Reiner...

335
00:26:32,540 --> 00:26:34,210
Don't tell me...

336
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:36,890
You're gonna jump out the window with it?!

337
00:26:36,890 --> 00:26:38,760
I've got no other choice!

338
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:39,810
Wait!

339
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:43,940
If I can just slice open its jaw...

340
00:26:45,290 --> 00:26:45,990
It let go!

341
00:26:54,610 --> 00:26:57,410
Sorry... I'm sorry.

342
00:26:57,410 --> 00:26:59,090
I think it's broken.

343
00:26:59,090 --> 00:27:01,860
Yeah, just my luck.

344
00:27:01,860 --> 00:27:03,340
I know.

345
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,390
Sorry...

346
00:27:08,410 --> 00:27:10,810
This dirty cloth is all I have.

347
00:27:11,090 --> 00:27:12,660
Sorry.

348
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:16,240
No, it helps.

349
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:18,690
<b><i>Marry me.</i></b>

350
00:27:25,190 --> 00:27:27,140
Everyone understand the plan?

351
00:27:27,140 --> 00:27:27,760
Yes, ma'am!

352
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:33,510
This is where we split up. I'm counting on you.

353
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:39,290
Erwin had to improvise with your group, but you're our only hope.

354
00:27:40,310 --> 00:27:42,210
Eren.

355
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:45,490
You need to rein yourself in.

356
00:27:45,490 --> 00:27:48,790
Don't let anger distract you from who you are.

357
00:27:48,790 --> 00:27:51,040
Don't buckle this time.

358
00:27:51,460 --> 00:27:52,540
Yes, sir!

359
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:57,860
We can see the wall from a tower near here.

360
00:27:57,860 --> 00:28:00,910
It's an old castle near the southwestern portion.

361
00:28:00,910 --> 00:28:03,360
We're headed for Utgard Castle.

362
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:18,610
That takes care of all the big ones.

363
00:28:18,610 --> 00:28:20,610
Thank goodness for this tower.

364
00:28:20,610 --> 00:28:23,340
Yeah, we might actually survive.

365
00:28:23,760 --> 00:28:25,760
I'll go check on the newbies.

366
00:28:29,010 --> 00:28:30,140
What's that sound?

367
00:28:35,310 --> 00:28:36,840
The horses!

368
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:39,190
Again?!

369
00:28:39,190 --> 00:28:40,890
What <b><i>is</i></b> that sound?

370
00:28:45,060 --> 00:28:47,410
Lynne! Henning!

371
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:54,360
What was that?

372
00:28:55,260 --> 00:28:56,590
It's no use.

373
00:28:56,590 --> 00:28:59,410
They both died instantly.

374
00:29:00,190 --> 00:29:01,560
This can't be...

375
00:29:02,660 --> 00:29:05,760
It was that thing! 
The one that climbed up for the wall!

376
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:08,740
That Beast Titan did this!

377
00:29:09,990 --> 00:29:13,010
A horde of Titans is closing in! 
At least twice as many as before!

378
00:29:13,010 --> 00:29:14,760
What?

379
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:18,190
With this timing, it's like they're following a strategy.

380
00:29:18,190 --> 00:29:22,310
Like they've been toying with us this entire time.

381
00:29:47,060 --> 00:29:49,790
<b><i>Crap, I'm almost out of gas!</i></b>

382
00:29:54,310 --> 00:29:55,260
Did I get it?

383
00:30:04,810 --> 00:30:07,260
This tower won't hold much longer.

384
00:30:07,260 --> 00:30:09,260
I only have a small amount of gas left.

385
00:30:09,790 --> 00:30:11,260
What about you?

386
00:30:11,260 --> 00:30:14,010
Out of gas and out of blades.

387
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:17,490
Those blunt ones the last you have left?

388
00:30:19,810 --> 00:30:22,940
How many did the four of us take out?

389
00:30:22,940 --> 00:30:26,160
Beats me. I didn't have time to count.

390
00:30:26,890 --> 00:30:31,340
I feel like I did pretty well.

391
00:30:31,340 --> 00:30:34,060
But before I go...

392
00:30:34,060 --> 00:30:37,610
...I wish I could have some alcohol.

393
00:30:37,610 --> 00:30:39,310
Gelgar...

394
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:43,190
Sorry, Nanaba.

395
00:30:43,190 --> 00:30:45,140
I hit my head...

396
00:30:45,140 --> 00:30:47,640
I can't hold...

397
00:30:47,640 --> 00:30:49,340
...any longer.

398
00:30:50,610 --> 00:30:51,810
Gelgar!

399
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,440
Gelgar!

400
00:31:08,060 --> 00:31:09,940
No! No!

401
00:31:09,940 --> 00:31:11,710
Father, stop!

402
00:31:11,710 --> 00:31:13,440
Father! I'm sorry!

403
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,440
No!

404
00:31:16,110 --> 00:31:17,840
Goddammit!

405
00:31:18,290 --> 00:31:23,160
Do we gotta wait here now until
the tower falls and we get eaten alive?

406
00:31:23,990 --> 00:31:29,360
We can't just die without accomplishing anything!

407
00:31:31,660 --> 00:31:34,340
I... want to fight, too.

408
00:31:34,340 --> 00:31:36,990
If only I had a weapon...

409
00:31:36,990 --> 00:31:39,560
Then I could fight and die alongside them.

410
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:43,660
Christa, you're still saying things like that?

411
00:31:44,010 --> 00:31:46,260
Don't you dare take advantage of their deaths.

412
00:31:46,260 --> 00:31:50,790
Our superiors didn't die to make your suicide look good.

413
00:31:51,810 --> 00:31:54,660
That's... That's not what I...

414
00:31:54,660 --> 00:31:57,240
You're not like Conny or the superiors!

415
00:31:58,090 --> 00:32:00,660
You aren't actually determined to survive.

416
00:32:01,210 --> 00:32:05,410
All you want to do is die in a way
that makes you seem like a hero.

417
00:32:05,810 --> 00:32:07,940
Th-That's not...

418
00:32:07,940 --> 00:32:11,460
Conny, give me that knife.

419
00:32:11,460 --> 00:32:13,310
Huh? Why?

420
00:32:13,310 --> 00:32:14,940
Just hand it over.

421
00:32:14,940 --> 00:32:17,240
Fine, here.

422
00:32:20,090 --> 00:32:21,460
Thanks, buddy.

423
00:32:21,460 --> 00:32:23,460
What're you planning on doing with it?

424
00:32:24,690 --> 00:32:26,690
What else?

425
00:32:28,340 --> 00:32:30,540
I'm gonna fight with it.

426
00:32:31,210 --> 00:32:33,560
Ymir... What are you planning?

427
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:37,690
Who knows? I don't even know myself.

428
00:32:38,340 --> 00:32:39,710
Ymir...

429
00:32:40,690 --> 00:32:45,690
Christa... This is probably it for us...

430
00:32:51,110 --> 00:32:52,340
Christa...

431
00:32:52,690 --> 00:32:54,440
Remember it for me.

432
00:32:55,500 --> 00:32:59,440
We made a promise during our training on that snowy mountain.

433
00:33:01,690 --> 00:33:02,610
You have to promise me.

434
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:06,300
When I reveal my secret,

435
00:33:06,740 --> 00:33:11,840
you need to go back to living under your real name.

436
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:26,410
Promise me, Christa.

437
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:29,690
Ymir! Wait!

438
00:33:32,190 --> 00:33:33,510
Ymir!

439
00:34:04,940 --> 00:34:06,690
That Titan...

440
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,690
It's from back then...

441
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:26,790
Thanks, Reiner.

442
00:34:26,790 --> 00:34:30,260
It hurts! Reiner, my leg!

443
00:34:30,260 --> 00:34:32,260
Reiner, that's enough!

444
00:34:32,660 --> 00:34:34,860
Let go of her leg! Her leg!

445
00:34:34,860 --> 00:34:36,690
Hey!

446
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:39,690
S-Sorry!

447
00:34:39,690 --> 00:34:41,890
It's okay. You saved me.

448
00:34:41,890 --> 00:34:45,040
Christa... Did you know?

449
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:48,810
That Ymir is a Titan?

450
00:34:50,110 --> 00:34:51,860
I had no idea.

451
00:34:51,860 --> 00:34:54,240
We've always stuck so close together,

452
00:34:54,240 --> 00:34:57,210
but I... I never would've imagined this.

453
00:34:58,910 --> 00:35:03,710
In other words, she knew 
some of the secrets of our world.

454
00:35:04,460 --> 00:35:07,790
I wonder... What could be Ymir's goal?

455
00:35:14,460 --> 00:35:15,640
Ymir!

456
00:35:40,460 --> 00:35:41,790
She's...

457
00:35:45,180 --> 00:35:46,590
Wh-What was that?

458
00:35:46,590 --> 00:35:50,060
Is she worried about bringing the tower down?

459
00:35:50,060 --> 00:35:51,340
She has to be.

460
00:35:51,340 --> 00:35:56,640
If she wanted to, she could've used her power to escape all on her own.

461
00:35:56,640 --> 00:35:59,440
And yet, she's not doing that.

462
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,690
Don't you die, Ymir!

463
00:36:06,690 --> 00:36:09,260
Quit playing the goody two-shoes, you idiot!

464
00:36:09,260 --> 00:36:13,380
You wanna go out in a blaze of glory? Are you stupid?!

465
00:36:13,790 --> 00:36:16,210
Live for yourself!

466
00:36:17,210 --> 00:36:21,110
If you're gonna die protecting 
this tower, then forget about it!

467
00:36:21,110 --> 00:36:23,610
Tear it down!

468
00:36:22,460 --> 00:36:23,610
Hey!

469
00:36:35,150 --> 00:36:38,210
H-Hey! She's really tearing it down!

470
00:36:38,210 --> 00:36:40,210
There you go, Ymir!

471
00:36:43,840 --> 00:36:45,560
Want to live?

472
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:46,960
Grab on!

473
00:37:19,650 --> 00:37:20,740
They're still alive...?

474
00:37:20,740 --> 00:37:23,910
Hey, ugly! Go and finish the job!

475
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:30,960
Ymir!

476
00:37:37,490 --> 00:37:38,660
This looks bad.

477
00:37:50,590 --> 00:37:51,760
Ymir is...

478
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:55,610
No...

479
00:37:56,310 --> 00:37:58,110
This can't...

480
00:37:59,540 --> 00:38:01,010
Christa!

481
00:38:01,010 --> 00:38:02,240
This can't...

482
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:04,490
Ymir, wait!

483
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:06,060
I still...

484
00:38:06,060 --> 00:38:08,460
...have something to tell you!

485
00:38:08,460 --> 00:38:09,290
I still...

486
00:38:09,690 --> 00:38:15,190
haven't told you my real name yet!

487
00:38:25,110 --> 00:38:26,460
<b><i>Wait...</i></b>

488
00:38:27,610 --> 00:38:28,960
<b><i>I still...</i></b>

489
00:38:38,060 --> 00:38:41,210
Christa. Everyone, get back.

490
00:38:42,210 --> 00:38:42,940
We'll handle this.

491
00:38:43,660 --> 00:38:45,160
Leave the rest to us.

492
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:46,240
Mikasa?

493
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:55,010
Rear guard, secure a perimeter!

494
00:38:55,010 --> 00:38:58,410
Everyone else, get to those Titans and bring 'em down!

495
00:38:58,410 --> 00:38:59,090
Yes, ma'am!

496
00:39:00,140 --> 00:39:00,910
Hey!

497
00:39:00,910 --> 00:39:03,510
You don't need to be a part of the attack!

498
00:39:05,090 --> 00:39:06,240
Die!

499
00:39:07,740 --> 00:39:09,960
I did it! My first kill!

500
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:17,560
Dumbass! There's a reason 
we told you to stay back, Eren!

501
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:19,560
Yes, sir! I'm sorry!

502
00:39:21,060 --> 00:39:23,940
Hey! Eren!

503
00:39:23,940 --> 00:39:25,440
You guys!

504
00:40:11,390 --> 00:40:15,040
Unbelievable... Ymir is...

505
00:40:20,410 --> 00:40:21,690
Ymir...

506
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:39,110
My real name...

507
00:40:39,110 --> 00:40:41,560
...is Historia.

508
00:41:24,610 --> 00:41:26,190
Reiner! Grab on!

509
00:41:26,610 --> 00:41:28,240
Right!

510
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:35,940
How's Ymir?

511
00:41:36,490 --> 00:41:38,640
She's still in a coma.

512
00:41:38,640 --> 00:41:42,960
The bleeding has stopped, and the wounds appear to be emitting steam...

513
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:48,640
For now, take her back to Trost District 
so she can get some proper medical care.

514
00:41:48,640 --> 00:41:49,810
You're on it.

515
00:41:49,810 --> 00:41:51,860
Yes, ma'am.

516
00:41:52,460 --> 00:41:53,860
Now then...

517
00:42:06,040 --> 00:42:08,540
Ow...

518
00:42:09,210 --> 00:42:11,040
You okay, Reiner?

519
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:13,260
Not by a long shot.

520
00:42:13,260 --> 00:42:15,990
A Titan bit into my arm.

521
00:42:15,990 --> 00:42:18,740
Man, this sucks.

522
00:42:18,740 --> 00:42:20,740
I thought I was done for.

523
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:29,790
Even someone as strong as you 
gets this way sometimes.

524
00:42:29,790 --> 00:42:33,210
What are you talking about? 
This is my second time!

525
00:42:33,210 --> 00:42:34,410
Right, Armin?

526
00:42:35,260 --> 00:42:38,890
I got squished inside a Titan's hand that one time.

527
00:42:40,510 --> 00:42:43,510
This is the second time I've stared death in the face.

528
00:42:43,510 --> 00:42:47,090
At this rate, I'll be dead before I know it.

529
00:42:47,090 --> 00:42:51,910
I picked this path on my own, 
but being a soldier is rough.

530
00:42:51,910 --> 00:42:55,210
I feel like my mind is gonna collapse before my body.

531
00:42:56,510 --> 00:42:59,560
Though, until we plug up this wall,

532
00:42:59,560 --> 00:43:01,610
there's no time to waste whining about it.

533
00:43:03,710 --> 00:43:08,140
You two have been driven 
far enough away from your hometown.

534
00:43:08,140 --> 00:43:11,490
I'm thinking... this is where 
we gotta draw the line.

535
00:43:13,490 --> 00:43:14,990
That's right, Reiner!

536
00:43:14,990 --> 00:43:16,700
Our hometown! Let's return!

537
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:19,440
Isn't it about time to go back?

538
00:43:19,510 --> 00:43:23,410
Compared to what we've already been through, 
it'll just be one more push!

539
00:43:24,540 --> 00:43:25,890
That's right.

540
00:43:25,890 --> 00:43:28,790
We're only one push away!

541
00:43:31,610 --> 00:43:34,340
What are you guys talking about?

542
00:43:38,290 --> 00:43:39,610
Thanks, Mikasa.

543
00:43:40,040 --> 00:43:41,440
Are you hurt?

544
00:43:41,440 --> 00:43:43,040
No, I'm fine.

545
00:43:43,040 --> 00:43:46,490
But Reiner got bitten, and Ymir's... well, look at her.

546
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:50,040
I can't believe Ymir was a Titan, too...

547
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:52,060
Sasha.

548
00:43:52,060 --> 00:43:53,510
Is everyone clear?

549
00:43:53,710 --> 00:43:56,310
We'll deal with Ymir later.

550
00:43:56,310 --> 00:44:01,360
For the time being, I want you to focus 
on the mission to repair the wall.

551
00:44:03,710 --> 00:44:04,940
Mr. Hannes?

552
00:44:05,140 --> 00:44:07,540
It's the Garrison Regiment's advance unit!

553
00:44:07,790 --> 00:44:09,740
They must be here to tell us where the hole is!

554
00:44:13,610 --> 00:44:15,140
There's no hole anywhere!

555
00:44:16,640 --> 00:44:19,240
We spent all night looking for it...

556
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:24,260
but between Trost District and Krolva District, there wasn't anything.

557
00:44:24,260 --> 00:44:25,510
What?

558
00:44:26,260 --> 00:44:29,440
Then we ran into the Krolva District soldiers and turned back.

559
00:44:30,190 --> 00:44:33,410
Fortunately, we didn't run into any Titans.

560
00:44:33,410 --> 00:44:37,440
But... there were definitely Titans on the inside!

561
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:40,940
Were you really looking? 
Are you sure you're not drunk?

562
00:44:40,940 --> 00:44:42,260
How could I be?

563
00:44:42,260 --> 00:44:45,260
Actually, wait, what are you lot doing here?

564
00:44:55,940 --> 00:44:58,990
If there's no hole in the wall, so be it.

565
00:44:58,990 --> 00:45:01,340
Stand by in Trost District for the time being!

566
00:45:05,240 --> 00:45:09,040
You guys still aren't completely safe.

567
00:45:09,640 --> 00:45:11,610
Don't let your guard down yet.

568
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:18,640
There's nothing?

569
00:45:18,640 --> 00:45:20,760
What could this mean?

570
00:45:21,190 --> 00:45:25,490
There's been nothing like this in 
five years. Why is it all happening now?

571
00:45:25,490 --> 00:45:28,510
This world is getting more 
and more out of hand.

572
00:45:28,510 --> 00:45:30,290
Eren.

573
00:45:30,290 --> 00:45:31,590
Have a minute?

574
00:45:31,590 --> 00:45:32,860
We need to talk.

575
00:45:33,810 --> 00:45:36,290
What is it?

576
00:45:36,290 --> 00:45:41,510
Five years ago, we destroyed the wall and attacked humanity.

577
00:45:41,510 --> 00:45:45,990
Oh no... What if there's a Titan 
that digs a hole underneath the wall?

578
00:45:45,990 --> 00:45:48,960
In that case, the hole 
would be very difficult to find.

579
00:45:48,960 --> 00:45:52,340
I'm the Armored Titan, 
and he's the Colossal Titan.

580
00:45:52,340 --> 00:45:56,390
For now, let's just focus 
on getting Ymir back safely.

581
00:45:56,390 --> 00:46:00,340
Even with our horses, we still have to worry about Titans.

582
00:46:01,690 --> 00:46:03,140
What are you talking about?

583
00:46:03,140 --> 00:46:05,460
What the hell are you doing, Reiner?

584
00:46:05,460 --> 00:46:10,140
Our goal was to ensure 
all of humanity was wiped out,

585
00:46:10,660 --> 00:46:13,540
but now there's no need for that.

586
00:46:14,540 --> 00:46:15,710
Eren,

587
00:46:15,710 --> 00:46:21,540
if you come with us, we won't have to destroy any more of the walls.

588
00:46:21,540 --> 00:46:22,740
You understand?

589
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:26,440
No, wait! I don't understand at all!

590
00:46:26,440 --> 00:46:30,540
I'm telling you to come with us.

591
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:35,160
Hey! We're leaving!

592
00:46:36,210 --> 00:46:38,060
<b><i>What a mess...</i></b>

593
00:46:38,510 --> 00:46:42,960
<b><i>And here I thought I had 
enough to think about yesterday...</i></b>

594
00:46:45,430 --> 00:46:47,840
12 Hours Earlier

595
00:46:48,550 --> 00:46:51,220
Ehrmich District

596
00:46:48,860 --> 00:46:49,860
Huh?

597
00:46:49,860 --> 00:46:51,890
Is something the matter, Hange?

598
00:46:52,610 --> 00:46:59,690
Well, I was finally able to get my hands on the background report for Annie Leonhart.

599
00:46:59,690 --> 00:47:08,010
According to this, there are two other 104th cadets from the same area as her.

600
00:47:08,490 --> 00:47:10,890
Their names are...

601
00:47:10,890 --> 00:47:12,640
Reiner Braun...

602
00:47:12,640 --> 00:47:13,940
...and Bertholdt Hoover.

603
00:47:16,360 --> 00:47:22,940
Because of the chaos five years ago, family records are a total mess.

604
00:47:22,940 --> 00:47:24,610
However...

605
00:47:24,610 --> 00:47:30,190
During the recent expedition outside the walls, 
their group was given false information.

606
00:47:30,190 --> 00:47:34,740
They were among those purposely told 
that Eren was in the right flank of the formation.

607
00:47:35,740 --> 00:47:38,710
That's where the Female Titan first appeared!

608
00:47:38,710 --> 00:47:40,790
Huh? What does that mean?

609
00:47:40,790 --> 00:47:45,060
It's possible they passed on 
that information to Annie...

610
00:47:45,060 --> 00:47:46,860
Hold on a minute, Armin.

611
00:47:47,440 --> 00:47:49,660
Putting aside Bertholdt, who doesn't say much,

612
00:47:49,660 --> 00:47:52,140
Reiner is like a big brother to us.

613
00:47:52,190 --> 00:47:53,790
He's not clever enough to deceive people.

614
00:47:53,790 --> 00:47:55,140
I know, Eren.

615
00:47:55,510 --> 00:47:58,760
That's not enough to prove anything.

616
00:47:59,340 --> 00:48:00,890
Everyone, listen up.

617
00:48:01,340 --> 00:48:06,490
If you run into Reiner or Bertholdt, 
don't let them realize we suspect them.

618
00:48:07,060 --> 00:48:11,660
And don't talk about Annie Leonhart at all.

619
00:48:11,660 --> 00:48:14,490
Whether they're in league with her or not,

620
00:48:14,490 --> 00:48:18,610
we need to lead them deep 
underground and confine them.

621
00:48:18,610 --> 00:48:20,290
Does everyone understand?

622
00:48:20,290 --> 00:48:21,110
Yes, ma'am!

623
00:48:22,190 --> 00:48:24,110
What the heck?

624
00:48:25,890 --> 00:48:28,290
You're just tired, aren't you?

625
00:48:28,290 --> 00:48:30,490
Right, Bertholdt?

626
00:48:30,490 --> 00:48:33,440
You've been through so much, it's making you crazy.

627
00:48:33,440 --> 00:48:35,290
Y-Yeah.

628
00:48:35,290 --> 00:48:37,140
Reiner's just really tired.

629
00:48:38,090 --> 00:48:43,060
Besides, if you were really the Armored Titan that killed so many people...

630
00:48:43,060 --> 00:48:45,690
...why would you be asking me 
this in the first place?

631
00:48:46,210 --> 00:48:51,640
What did you think would happen? 
That I'd nod and say "Sure, let's go"?

632
00:49:02,890 --> 00:49:04,310
Oh, right.

633
00:49:04,910 --> 00:49:07,510
That's right.

634
00:49:07,510 --> 00:49:10,210
What the hell was I thinking?

635
00:49:11,840 --> 00:49:14,810
Have I really gone crazy?

636
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:18,990
Come on, let's go.

637
00:49:50,360 --> 00:49:52,190
I know...

638
00:49:53,310 --> 00:49:55,640
Surely...

639
00:49:56,340 --> 00:49:59,710
I've been here too long for my own good.

640
00:50:01,490 --> 00:50:07,590
It's been three long years, 
surrounded by nothing but idiots.

641
00:50:07,590 --> 00:50:12,060
We were just kids. 
We didn't know anything.

642
00:50:13,740 --> 00:50:18,140
If only I hadn't known that you idiots existed,

643
00:50:18,140 --> 00:50:20,140
I...

644
00:50:20,640 --> 00:50:23,190
never would've become...

645
00:50:23,190 --> 00:50:26,160
such a half-hearted piece of shit!

646
00:50:28,410 --> 00:50:33,040
I don't know what's right and what's wrong anymore.

647
00:50:33,290 --> 00:50:36,640
But the only choice for me now...

648
00:50:36,640 --> 00:50:40,690
is to face the consequences of my actions...

649
00:50:41,090 --> 00:50:46,960
...and fulfill my duty to the bitter end as a Warrior!

650
00:50:51,740 --> 00:50:52,660
Reiner!

651
00:50:52,910 --> 00:50:55,990
Are we doing it? Right here, right now?

652
00:50:55,990 --> 00:50:57,040
Yeah.

653
00:50:57,040 --> 00:51:00,240
We'll settle everything right here!

654
00:51:13,110 --> 00:51:14,160
Eren!

655
00:51:14,160 --> 00:51:15,210
Run!

656
00:51:18,410 --> 00:51:19,610
Bertholdt!

657
00:51:25,490 --> 00:51:27,890
Eren! Run!

658
00:51:52,140 --> 00:51:52,890
Eren!

659
00:52:04,890 --> 00:52:07,830
<b><i>I'm going to return to my lost hometown.</i></b>

660
00:52:07,830 --> 00:52:10,710
<b><i>That's the only thing that fuels me.</i></b>

661
00:52:15,510 --> 00:52:17,540
<b><i>Bertholdt...</i></b>

662
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:19,440
<b><i>Reiner...</i></b>

663
00:52:23,540 --> 00:52:28,940
<b><i>You fucking traitors!</i></b>

664
00:52:37,690 --> 00:52:39,040
Eren!

665
00:52:41,190 --> 00:52:43,240
All troops, get off the wall!

666
00:52:53,990 --> 00:52:56,110
It got Ymir!

667
00:52:56,110 --> 00:52:58,240
And someone else, too!

668
00:53:03,540 --> 00:53:06,140
All troops, prepare for combat!

669
00:53:06,140 --> 00:53:08,610
We're taking down the Colossal Titan!

670
00:53:08,990 --> 00:53:11,560
It's the greatest threat to all of mankind!

671
00:53:11,560 --> 00:53:13,560
Everyone attack at once!

672
00:53:30,590 --> 00:53:33,490
<b><i>The reports were right! He's slow!</i></b>

673
00:53:33,490 --> 00:53:35,460
<b><i>It might be big, but that's it!</i></b>

674
00:53:35,460 --> 00:53:38,990
<b><i>It's nothing compared to 
the Titans we usually fight!</i></b>

675
00:53:39,290 --> 00:53:42,560
Now's our chance! Slice up his neck!

676
00:53:46,890 --> 00:53:48,040
Too hot!

677
00:53:48,340 --> 00:53:50,390
All troops, pull back!

678
00:53:59,210 --> 00:54:01,640
He's trying to disappear again?

679
00:54:01,640 --> 00:54:04,140
No, something is different.

680
00:54:04,140 --> 00:54:06,140
In the past, he vanished instantly,

681
00:54:06,140 --> 00:54:11,360
but now, he's maintaining his form 
and emitting heat like a furnace.

682
00:54:11,360 --> 00:54:13,840
If he keeps protecting himself with steam...

683
00:54:17,240 --> 00:54:19,210
We can't attack him with ODM gear!

684
00:54:19,590 --> 00:54:22,140
Wh-What do we do?

685
00:54:22,140 --> 00:54:25,190
We can't do anything. We wait.

686
00:54:25,510 --> 00:54:29,040
I don't know how long he can keep his body burning,

687
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:30,740
but he has to come out eventually.

688
00:54:31,240 --> 00:54:33,760
We wait for that moment to attack.

689
00:54:33,760 --> 00:54:35,540
Listen up.

690
00:54:35,540 --> 00:54:37,460
Capturing them alive is no longer an option.

691
00:54:37,460 --> 00:54:38,910
Kill them.

692
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:39,960
And don't hesitate!

693
00:54:43,510 --> 00:54:47,040
Armin and First Squad, follow me!

694
00:54:47,310 --> 00:54:49,090
We'll deal with the Armored Titan!

695
00:55:12,690 --> 00:55:13,990
<b><i>That did nothing!</i></b>

696
00:55:15,090 --> 00:55:16,610
<b><i>Eren's attacks...</i></b>

697
00:55:16,610 --> 00:55:18,610
<b><i>and my blades aren't working!</i></b>

698
00:55:19,610 --> 00:55:23,110
<b><i>What's worse, unlike Annie, 
his whole body is hard!</i></b>

699
00:55:26,360 --> 00:55:28,360
Eren!

700
00:55:31,360 --> 00:55:33,840
<b><i>Hey, Reiner...</i></b>

701
00:55:34,710 --> 00:55:39,360
<b><i>I don't know what kind of face 
you're making right now,</i></b>

702
00:55:44,610 --> 00:55:49,460
<b><i>But you two really are 
the worst pieces of shit.</i></b>

703
00:55:50,610 --> 00:55:53,340
<b><i>Seriously, what the hell are you thinking?</i></b>

704
00:55:53,340 --> 00:55:55,790
<b><i>You really disgust me.</i></b>

705
00:55:55,790 --> 00:56:00,290
<b><i>Just remembering you and your 
self-righteous face is making me sick.</i></b>

706
00:56:02,360 --> 00:56:08,490
<b><i>It makes me want to vomit, 
you big damn pest!</i></b>

707
00:56:09,960 --> 00:56:12,760
<b><i>I'll exterminate you right here!</i></b>

708
00:56:35,190 --> 00:56:36,990
He threw the Armored Titan!

709
00:56:36,990 --> 00:56:39,090
Wait... Isn't that...

710
00:56:39,090 --> 00:56:41,090
the technique Annie used?

711
00:56:51,160 --> 00:56:54,010
<b><i>I did it! Submissions work on him!</i></b>

712
00:56:54,010 --> 00:56:56,110
<b><i>I still have a chance!</i></b>

713
00:57:00,360 --> 00:57:01,690
<b><i>I'm not done yet!</i></b>

714
00:57:05,490 --> 00:57:07,060
Eren!

715
00:57:07,060 --> 00:57:09,640
<b><i>You're not getting away so easy!</i></b>

716
00:57:25,860 --> 00:57:27,960
He did it!

717
00:57:35,010 --> 00:57:37,510
Eren! Can you hear me?!

718
00:57:37,510 --> 00:57:40,490
Run away! At least get back to the wall!

719
00:57:40,490 --> 00:57:44,240
Their goal is to kidnap and take you away!

720
00:57:44,240 --> 00:57:47,510
We need to prioritize preventing that!

721
00:57:47,510 --> 00:57:51,710
But Armin, I don't think Reiner's going to let him get away so easily.

722
00:57:55,210 --> 00:57:58,060
It's dangerous here! Get back, you two!

723
00:58:23,410 --> 00:58:25,760
There you go! Good decision!

724
00:58:27,210 --> 00:58:27,960
Mikasa!

725
00:58:28,240 --> 00:58:30,560
Take my blades. You need them.

726
00:58:44,640 --> 00:58:45,590
He's fast!

727
00:58:50,140 --> 00:58:51,210
<b><i>Shit!</i></b>

728
00:58:51,210 --> 00:58:52,810
<b><i>The legs! Go for the legs!</i></b>

729
00:58:56,040 --> 00:58:58,210
Don't let him get on top of you!

730
00:58:58,210 --> 00:58:59,110
Stand up!

731
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:08,810
<b><i>If I'm going down either way,</i></b>

732
00:59:08,810 --> 00:59:10,990
<b><i>then fine.</i></b>

733
00:59:10,990 --> 00:59:13,510
<b><i>Just give me...</i></b>

734
00:59:13,510 --> 00:59:15,890
<b><i>...your neck!</i></b>

735
00:59:19,860 --> 00:59:23,110
<b><i>Got him! Now it's just a battle of strength!</i></b>

736
00:59:28,410 --> 00:59:29,270
<b><i>This freak...</i></b>

737
00:59:31,040 --> 00:59:31,690
<b><i>He's still...</i></b>

738
00:59:41,690 --> 00:59:42,710
<b><i>Mikasa...</i></b>

739
00:59:44,040 --> 00:59:44,940
She got him!

740
00:59:50,960 --> 00:59:53,810
<b><i>His resistance is weakening!</i></b>

741
01:00:02,360 --> 01:00:04,090
You've got this!

742
01:00:04,090 --> 01:00:05,240
Get him, Eren!

743
01:00:05,240 --> 01:00:07,840
Rip his whole head off!

744
01:00:07,840 --> 01:00:10,560
Drag that traitor outta there!

745
01:00:12,790 --> 01:00:14,610
<b><i>I can win.</i></b>

746
01:00:14,610 --> 01:00:17,890
<b><i>I can beat Reiner!</i></b>

747
01:00:30,360 --> 01:00:32,060
What's he doing?

748
01:00:32,060 --> 01:00:34,060
Panicking.

749
01:00:34,060 --> 01:00:36,190
Keep it up! Just a little more!

750
01:00:45,910 --> 01:00:47,410
He stopped.

751
01:00:49,560 --> 01:00:50,790
But why there?

752
01:01:06,860 --> 01:01:08,390
Watch the surroundings!

753
01:01:08,390 --> 01:01:09,960
He's calling for Titans!

754
01:01:18,140 --> 01:01:20,890
There are no Titans nearby!

755
01:01:20,890 --> 01:01:22,310
He's truly desperate!

756
01:01:22,710 --> 01:01:25,690
Try screaming for help with 
your head ripped off, dumbass!

757
01:01:25,690 --> 01:01:27,860
Look! He's coming apart!

758
01:01:28,710 --> 01:01:30,840
What's with the Armored Titan?

759
01:01:30,840 --> 01:01:33,240
Why'd he scream like that?

760
01:01:42,340 --> 01:01:43,960
Whoa...

761
01:01:43,960 --> 01:01:45,960
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

762
01:01:58,590 --> 01:02:01,660
Above you! Get out of there!

763
01:02:12,480 --> 01:02:16,150
Trost District

764
01:02:24,460 --> 01:02:25,690
Commander.

765
01:02:26,810 --> 01:02:29,590
Commander Pyxis, please wake up.

766
01:02:30,590 --> 01:02:32,740
You'll get sick if you fall asleep here.

767
01:02:34,060 --> 01:02:36,810
How'd you drink so much?

768
01:02:36,810 --> 01:02:39,190
You're not young anymore.

769
01:02:39,190 --> 01:02:43,140
And I'd rather not spend my days 
changing your diapers.

770
01:02:43,140 --> 01:02:47,160
Being cared for by a pretty lady 
sounds all right to me.

771
01:02:47,160 --> 01:02:48,960
So? What's the situation?

772
01:02:50,960 --> 01:02:52,860
They've been looking for Titans

773
01:02:52,860 --> 01:02:56,660
ever since they stopped appearing at the first and second lines of defense,

774
01:02:56,660 --> 01:02:59,940
but hardly any have been found.

775
01:03:01,510 --> 01:03:05,590
If Squad Hannes, our vanguard, 
inspected the wall without incident,

776
01:03:05,590 --> 01:03:07,840
then they should be back any time now.

777
01:03:09,590 --> 01:03:10,910
Commander Pyxis.

778
01:03:12,660 --> 01:03:14,560
Oh, Erwin.

779
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:19,690
I hear you caught one of those rats.

780
01:03:19,690 --> 01:03:20,940
Yes.

781
01:03:20,940 --> 01:03:23,740
Unfortunately, we were one step behind.

782
01:03:25,790 --> 01:03:29,810
Still, that's enough to get those in the interior thinking.

783
01:03:29,810 --> 01:03:35,230
Now they have to decide if they want to die with their old-fashioned traditions.

784
01:03:35,390 --> 01:03:39,840
Yes, that seems to be the case. Look.

785
01:03:40,060 --> 01:03:45,690
The Military Police Regiment has finally 
been forced into an area with Titans.

786
01:03:47,310 --> 01:03:50,490
Can you believe it? 
I thought this was an emergency.

787
01:03:50,490 --> 01:03:53,410
Yeah. And everyone's just sitting around here.

788
01:03:53,410 --> 01:03:56,640
Hey, Levi, where's our prey?

789
01:03:57,390 --> 01:04:01,090
Oh? You all seem so disappointed.

790
01:04:01,840 --> 01:04:05,560
Sorry that I couldn't set you up with any Titans.

791
01:04:05,560 --> 01:04:11,410
If you're looking for another chance, there are plenty of expeditions outside the walls.

792
01:04:12,140 --> 01:04:16,040
How about we join forces 
and face some Titans together?

793
01:04:18,160 --> 01:04:20,960
The vanguard has returned!

794
01:04:20,960 --> 01:04:23,160
Someone tell Commander Pyxis!

795
01:04:45,310 --> 01:04:46,510
Mikasa?

796
01:04:47,190 --> 01:04:49,060
Armin, where's Eren?

797
01:04:49,060 --> 01:04:51,360
Mikasa, calm down!

798
01:04:51,360 --> 01:04:52,440
Stop moving around!

799
01:04:52,440 --> 01:04:55,040
We don't know how bad your injuries are!

800
01:05:04,840 --> 01:05:06,140
Where is he?!

801
01:05:07,340 --> 01:05:08,990
Eren was taken away.

802
01:05:12,690 --> 01:05:15,040
Eren...

803
01:05:15,040 --> 01:05:17,390
lost to the Armored Titan.

804
01:05:19,690 --> 01:05:22,940
Bertholdt and Reiner. 
They took Ymir, too.

805
01:05:26,390 --> 01:05:29,340
It's been five hours since then.

806
01:05:31,240 --> 01:05:32,890
Did anyone...

807
01:05:32,890 --> 01:05:34,890
...go after them?

808
01:05:37,460 --> 01:05:38,260
No.

809
01:05:38,260 --> 01:05:40,260
Why not?!

810
01:05:42,410 --> 01:05:45,760
We can't get the horses to the other side of the wall.

811
01:05:48,190 --> 01:05:49,790
In order to rescue Eren,

812
01:05:49,790 --> 01:05:54,160
we have to wait for lifts to come so we can transport the horses over the wall.

813
01:05:54,160 --> 01:05:56,160
You need to be ready for that.

814
01:05:57,340 --> 01:06:01,710
Section Commander Hange and 
the other officers are too injured to move.

815
01:06:01,710 --> 01:06:06,810
We need every soldier we can get 
to make even a small scout squad.

816
01:06:07,540 --> 01:06:08,960
Especially skilled ones.

817
01:06:10,460 --> 01:06:12,060
You understand?

818
01:06:24,090 --> 01:06:26,510
Hey, Armin.

819
01:06:27,490 --> 01:06:28,360
Why...

820
01:06:29,410 --> 01:06:33,360
...does Eren always go 
somewhere far away from us?

821
01:06:34,540 --> 01:06:37,860
Yeah, now that you mention it.

822
01:06:39,390 --> 01:06:43,310
All I wanted was to be with him.

823
01:06:49,060 --> 01:06:51,060
That's all.

824
01:07:02,810 --> 01:07:05,360
Hey, Mikasa. Glad you're awake.

825
01:07:06,290 --> 01:07:09,210
You're hungry, right? Eat this.

826
01:07:10,810 --> 01:07:13,090
You too, Armin.

827
01:07:14,190 --> 01:07:18,340
As usual, field rations are all there is.

828
01:07:23,740 --> 01:07:27,410
Taste neither good nor bad. Same as always.

829
01:07:32,960 --> 01:07:35,560
Speaking of which, 
this is the same as always, too.

830
01:07:36,110 --> 01:07:42,310
Ever since the good old days, you two have 
been there to clean up the mess of that brat.

831
01:07:42,310 --> 01:07:45,990
Like it or not, that's how it is.

832
01:07:46,390 --> 01:07:49,790
The times and the situation might be totally different,

833
01:07:49,790 --> 01:07:53,360
but you kids are doing the same thing you always have.

834
01:07:56,190 --> 01:07:59,360
That brat isn't 
even all that good at fighting.

835
01:07:59,360 --> 01:08:04,140
But no matter if he's up against three or five, 
he'll charge in all the same.

836
01:08:04,490 --> 01:08:09,460
By the time Mikasa or a soldier was able to stop him, he'd already be black and blue.

837
01:08:10,660 --> 01:08:11,610
Thing is, though...

838
01:08:13,640 --> 01:08:16,360
While I've never seen him win a fight before,

839
01:08:16,360 --> 01:08:19,910
I've never seen him give up, either.

840
01:08:23,240 --> 01:08:28,410
Sometimes, he's so fierce he even scares me.

841
01:08:28,410 --> 01:08:31,810
He'll get right back up every time you knock him down.

842
01:08:32,210 --> 01:08:33,940
That's the kinda guy he is.

843
01:08:33,940 --> 01:08:37,940
You think he'll get taken away 
without putting up a fight?

844
01:08:37,940 --> 01:08:42,040
Nope. He'll keep resisting 
as long as he has strength.

845
01:08:42,040 --> 01:08:44,810
Seriously, he's only got two opponents!

846
01:08:45,110 --> 01:08:48,540
He'll give 'em hell no matter who he's up against.

847
01:08:48,540 --> 01:08:50,540
Until you or I show up to help.

848
01:08:51,190 --> 01:08:53,210
That's how Eren's always been!

849
01:09:00,960 --> 01:09:04,740
I loved those good old days.

850
01:09:04,740 --> 01:09:10,840
If you ask Eren, he'd say those days 
were nothing more than a false peace.

851
01:09:11,560 --> 01:09:17,490
But for me, I'm more than happy 
to be a drunk, useless soldier.

852
01:09:18,140 --> 01:09:21,990
If it means getting back to 
those plain, ordinary days...

853
01:09:21,990 --> 01:09:24,010
I'll do whatever I have to.

854
01:09:24,890 --> 01:09:27,510
No matter how long it takes to get there.

855
01:09:29,240 --> 01:09:31,160
I'm going, too.

856
01:09:31,160 --> 01:09:37,040
Without you three together again, 
I can't bring back the good old days.

857
01:10:06,140 --> 01:10:07,040
They're here.

858
01:10:08,190 --> 01:10:09,360
Hey.

859
01:10:09,360 --> 01:10:11,090
That's...

860
01:10:13,090 --> 01:10:14,810
Commander Erwin!

861
01:10:14,810 --> 01:10:16,810
And the Military Police Regiment!

862
01:10:23,560 --> 01:10:26,260
Commander Erwin, you made it!

863
01:10:26,260 --> 01:10:27,910
Is the situation the same?

864
01:10:27,910 --> 01:10:28,810
Yes, sir.

865
01:10:28,810 --> 01:10:29,960
Good.

866
01:10:29,960 --> 01:10:31,960
Deploy the lifts!

867
01:10:33,090 --> 01:10:34,760
Hange?!

868
01:10:34,760 --> 01:10:36,190
Moblit...

869
01:10:36,190 --> 01:10:37,760
G-Gimme a map.

870
01:10:44,490 --> 01:10:48,360
It's small, but there's a forest of giant trees here.

871
01:10:48,360 --> 01:10:50,740
You should head straight for it.

872
01:10:50,740 --> 01:10:51,490
Why's that?

873
01:10:52,240 --> 01:10:55,990
It's a gamble, but even if 
they are able to turn into Titans,

874
01:10:55,990 --> 01:11:00,290
the other Titans outside the walls 
might still be a threat to them.

875
01:11:00,440 --> 01:11:03,010
Especially after all that fighting.

876
01:11:03,010 --> 01:11:08,090
They might not be as bad off as Eren, 
but I'm sure they're exhausted.

877
01:11:08,090 --> 01:11:13,460
Which means they'll want to rest somewhere 
where Titans are unable to reach them.

878
01:11:13,890 --> 01:11:16,410
Until nightfall, when Titans can't move.

879
01:11:41,660 --> 01:11:43,390
Oh, Eren.

880
01:11:47,410 --> 01:11:48,860
You're awake?

881
01:12:00,540 --> 01:12:02,310
What theâ€”

882
01:12:02,310 --> 01:12:04,020
My arms!

883
01:12:04,020 --> 01:12:05,990
That was my fault.

884
01:12:05,990 --> 01:12:10,550
I was in a hurry, so when I bit you out of your Titan,

885
01:12:10,700 --> 01:12:13,360
I accidentally got your arms.

886
01:12:16,560 --> 01:12:18,510
Oh.

887
01:12:18,510 --> 01:12:21,710
I lost.

888
01:12:25,860 --> 01:12:27,210
Eren, stop!

889
01:12:27,640 --> 01:12:29,940
Don't be hasty, Eren.

890
01:12:29,940 --> 01:12:32,010
Take a good look around us.

891
01:12:32,510 --> 01:12:35,890
We're in the forest of giant trees inside Wall Maria.

892
01:12:35,890 --> 01:12:38,940
It's not even close to any of the walls.

893
01:12:39,740 --> 01:12:43,640
In other words, we're 
deep in Titan territory.

894
01:12:43,910 --> 01:12:46,140
And then there's <b><i>them</i></b>.

895
01:12:46,140 --> 01:12:51,810
Those stingy bastards 
are hogging the ODM gears.

896
01:12:51,810 --> 01:12:54,110
Reiner's wearing yours.

897
01:12:54,590 --> 01:12:58,690
Randomly transforming probably isn't gonna do us any good.

898
01:12:59,490 --> 01:13:03,460
I know that you're not going 
to listen and do as I say.

899
01:13:03,460 --> 01:13:08,160
But like Ymir was saying, 
this place is swarming with Titans.

900
01:13:08,160 --> 01:13:10,390
We could beat the shit out of each other right now,

901
01:13:10,390 --> 01:13:14,160
but when we're weak, the other Titans 
would just come and eat us.

902
01:13:14,860 --> 01:13:19,990
So until nightfall, when the Titans can't move, 
we have no choice but to wait here.

903
01:13:19,990 --> 01:13:23,740
Whether you two manage to escape from us...

904
01:13:23,740 --> 01:13:26,690
or we manage to carry you off...

905
01:13:26,960 --> 01:13:29,110
we have to wait until night.

906
01:13:51,960 --> 01:13:55,040
Reiner, you got any water?

907
01:13:55,040 --> 01:13:58,510
If I don't get some soon, 
I'm going to dry up and die.

908
01:13:58,510 --> 01:14:01,510
I know it's a matter of life and death,

909
01:14:01,510 --> 01:14:03,760
there's nothing we can do in this situation.

910
01:14:05,060 --> 01:14:09,510
You're right about that. 
This situation couldn't be any shittier.

911
01:14:12,340 --> 01:14:13,690
Speaking of which...

912
01:14:13,690 --> 01:14:16,460
Ever since the Titans 
showed up yesterday morning,

913
01:14:16,460 --> 01:14:19,310
we've been working our asses off.

914
01:14:19,910 --> 01:14:23,190
With nothing to eat or drink, 
and not even a wink of sleep.

915
01:14:24,010 --> 01:14:27,460
Well, at least the walls 
weren't broken or anything.

916
01:14:28,090 --> 01:14:30,290
I think we deserve to take a break for once.

917
01:14:30,990 --> 01:14:34,260
We'll see about getting promoted later.

918
01:14:34,260 --> 01:14:34,940
Reiner.

919
01:14:35,210 --> 01:14:38,990
Actually, we've done plenty 
enough to deserve consideration.

920
01:14:38,990 --> 01:14:43,190
We did pretty well, considering the crazy situation.

921
01:14:43,190 --> 01:14:50,240
I think they could spare us soldiers a little recognition for that, you know?

922
01:14:54,960 --> 01:14:59,790
Excuse me, Reiner, but what the hell?

923
01:14:59,790 --> 01:15:01,060
What do you mean?

924
01:15:01,060 --> 01:15:04,360
I'm not saying I wanna jump straight to Captain.

925
01:15:04,360 --> 01:15:06,610
That's not what I'm talking about.

926
01:15:06,610 --> 01:15:10,060
Oh, yeah. Where did you 
all get that cannon from?

927
01:15:10,060 --> 01:15:12,610
That really saved my ass.

928
01:15:13,040 --> 01:15:16,140
And then Christa patched me up.

929
01:15:16,140 --> 01:15:18,610
She's gotta have a thing for me, right?

930
01:15:18,610 --> 01:15:19,430
Hey.

931
01:15:19,430 --> 01:15:22,440
Now that I think about it, Christa has always treated me especiallyâ€”

932
01:15:22,440 --> 01:15:24,020
Hey!

933
01:15:27,540 --> 01:15:30,740
Are you fucking kidding me?

934
01:15:34,860 --> 01:15:36,490
What are you so angry about, Eren?

935
01:15:36,490 --> 01:15:39,660
Did I say something wrong?

936
01:15:39,660 --> 01:15:42,740
If you want to die, just keep talking!

937
01:15:42,740 --> 01:15:44,740
Hang on, Eren.

938
01:15:44,740 --> 01:15:47,040
This isn't normal, no matter how you look at it.

939
01:15:47,390 --> 01:15:49,660
Right, Bertholdt?

940
01:15:51,310 --> 01:15:56,160
If you know something, quit with the silence and come out and say it.

941
01:15:59,690 --> 01:16:01,390
Reiner...

942
01:16:01,390 --> 01:16:05,440
You're... not a soldier.

943
01:16:06,840 --> 01:16:08,510
We are...

944
01:16:08,510 --> 01:16:10,790
...Warriors.

945
01:16:21,040 --> 01:16:21,890
<b><i>Reiner!</i></b>

946
01:16:22,290 --> 01:16:23,760
<b><i>What are you doing?!</i></b>

947
01:16:29,140 --> 01:16:30,200
<b><i>Hey...</i></b>

948
01:16:30,750 --> 01:16:31,990
<b><i>Why...</i></b>

949
01:16:34,640 --> 01:16:37,210
<b><i>is Marco...</i></b>

950
01:16:37,210 --> 01:16:39,210
<b><i>...getting eaten?</i></b>

951
01:16:47,090 --> 01:16:48,740
Right.

952
01:16:48,740 --> 01:16:51,390
That's... right.

953
01:17:00,540 --> 01:17:03,260
What's with him?

954
01:17:03,260 --> 01:17:05,260
I thought it was strange.

955
01:17:05,260 --> 01:17:09,660
Why would the guy who destroyed 
the wall risk his life to save Conny?

956
01:17:09,660 --> 01:17:14,240
Everything he does is contradictory, 
but he doesn't realize it himself.

957
01:17:14,560 --> 01:17:15,910
No...

958
01:17:15,910 --> 01:17:18,790
Maybe he couldn't handle the weight of his sins,

959
01:17:18,790 --> 01:17:25,310
he convinced himself he was a soldier 
protecting the walls to keep his mind balanced.

960
01:17:25,310 --> 01:17:32,490
As a result, his heart was split 
and his memories were broken.

961
01:17:32,490 --> 01:17:36,590
Judging by Bertholdt's expression, this mustn't be the first time Reiner's made no sense.

962
01:17:36,590 --> 01:17:38,440
That's pretty incredible!

963
01:17:38,440 --> 01:17:40,810
For someone excessively honest like you toâ€”

964
01:17:40,810 --> 01:17:41,860
Shut up!

965
01:17:43,460 --> 01:17:45,740
Shut your mouth.

966
01:17:48,890 --> 01:17:50,490
My bad.

967
01:17:50,490 --> 01:17:52,010
I might have pried too much.

968
01:17:56,540 --> 01:17:58,660
You've gotta be kidding me.

969
01:18:00,040 --> 01:18:03,360
Why are you playing the victim here?

970
01:18:03,360 --> 01:18:05,460
What's your deal?

971
01:18:05,910 --> 01:18:10,060
I told you everything... 
while you looked at me right in the eyes...

972
01:18:10,060 --> 01:18:13,490
About how my mother was eaten alive...

973
01:18:13,490 --> 01:18:15,210
Isn't that right?

974
01:18:15,210 --> 01:18:19,360
I told you about how part of the gate you kicked in landed on my house,

975
01:18:19,360 --> 01:18:22,590
my mother couldn't run away.

976
01:18:22,590 --> 01:18:25,160
What were you thinking?

977
01:18:25,790 --> 01:18:29,610
What were you thinking when I told you all that?

978
01:18:31,910 --> 01:18:33,840
Back then...

979
01:18:35,260 --> 01:18:38,760
I felt very sorry for you.

980
01:18:41,740 --> 01:18:43,810
Oh.

981
01:18:44,390 --> 01:18:45,840
I get it.

982
01:18:47,210 --> 01:18:48,490
You guys...

983
01:18:49,190 --> 01:18:54,440
You guys... are neither soldiers or warriors.

984
01:18:54,440 --> 01:18:56,660
You're just murderers.

985
01:18:57,060 --> 01:19:02,060
You're psychotic mass-murderers 
who've killed countless innocent people!

986
01:19:02,060 --> 01:19:04,140
We know that!

987
01:19:04,140 --> 01:19:06,640
You think we need you to tell us?

988
01:19:06,640 --> 01:19:10,240
Then don't pretend to have 
emotions like you're one of us!

989
01:19:10,240 --> 01:19:12,590
You guys aren't even human anymore!

990
01:19:12,590 --> 01:19:15,710
It's you two who've turned 
this world into a living hell!

991
01:19:15,710 --> 01:19:17,490
Don't you understand that, you murderers?!

992
01:19:17,490 --> 01:19:21,360
So what do you want these murderers to do?!

993
01:19:21,360 --> 01:19:22,910
Do you want us to repent?

994
01:19:22,910 --> 01:19:24,460
Do you want us to apologize?!

995
01:19:24,460 --> 01:19:25,940
Will that satisfy you?

996
01:19:26,210 --> 01:19:28,940
We aren't the people you used to know!

997
01:19:28,940 --> 01:19:31,150
If yelling at us is gonna make you feel better,

998
01:19:31,150 --> 01:19:33,910
then go ahead and scream yourself hoarse!

999
01:19:46,910 --> 01:19:49,060
That's right...

1000
01:19:50,140 --> 01:19:52,290
I was still...

1001
01:19:52,290 --> 01:19:54,290
too naive.

1002
01:19:55,790 --> 01:19:57,460
I...

1003
01:19:57,460 --> 01:19:59,890
can only do my best now.

1004
01:19:59,890 --> 01:20:01,490
Do my best...

1005
01:20:02,440 --> 01:20:07,390
to make you two die in the 
most painful death possible.

1006
01:20:07,390 --> 01:20:08,760
I'll make sure of it.

1007
01:20:17,240 --> 01:20:18,940
That's not it.

1008
01:20:21,240 --> 01:20:23,040
Come on, Eren.

1009
01:20:23,040 --> 01:20:26,690
If you keep saying childish crap like that, 
I've got no faith in you.

1010
01:20:31,240 --> 01:20:32,990
Hey, Reiner.

1011
01:20:33,510 --> 01:20:36,290
What was that monkey?

1012
01:20:38,290 --> 01:20:40,660
Monkey? What do you mean?

1013
01:20:40,660 --> 01:20:42,960
Hmm? You don't know?

1014
01:20:43,560 --> 01:20:46,290
That's surprising, given how much you two

1015
01:20:46,290 --> 01:20:49,810
stared at it with stars in your 
eyes like two little brats.

1016
01:20:50,040 --> 01:20:51,140
That monkey...

1017
01:20:52,390 --> 01:20:55,440
What is a "monkey"?

1018
01:20:55,440 --> 01:20:56,760
Listen.

1019
01:20:57,290 --> 01:21:02,610
That monkey, the Beast Titan, 
is the root of the problem this time around.

1020
01:21:02,610 --> 01:21:05,210
It made Titans appear inside the walls.

1021
01:21:05,890 --> 01:21:09,210
I wonder if it was testing our strength.

1022
01:21:09,340 --> 01:21:12,290
These two are trying to get to it.

1023
01:21:12,870 --> 01:21:16,590
You know something? 
Tell me everything!

1024
01:21:16,590 --> 01:21:19,790
Calm down. There's a lot going on with me, too.

1025
01:21:19,790 --> 01:21:22,410
What the hell do you mean by that?!

1026
01:21:22,410 --> 01:21:26,110
Eren, if you think taking care of 
these two will bring an end to everything,

1027
01:21:26,560 --> 01:21:28,390
you're dead wrong.

1028
01:21:29,610 --> 01:21:31,460
Then who's the enemy?!

1029
01:21:31,460 --> 01:21:34,510
Enemy? If I tell you that, you'llâ€”

1030
01:21:34,510 --> 01:21:35,860
Ymir!

1031
01:21:35,860 --> 01:21:38,710
Do you think this world has a future?

1032
01:21:39,790 --> 01:21:43,740
If you know so much, 
think about what you want to do.

1033
01:21:43,740 --> 01:21:47,190
Surely you can consider coming over to our side.

1034
01:21:47,790 --> 01:21:49,860
And trust you?

1035
01:21:49,860 --> 01:21:53,390
Yeah, right. You two don't even trust me.

1036
01:21:53,390 --> 01:21:55,960
Wrong. We can trust you.

1037
01:21:56,410 --> 01:21:57,790
Because your one goal...

1038
01:21:58,790 --> 01:22:01,340
...is to protect Christa.

1039
01:22:02,810 --> 01:22:07,090
When it comes to that, we can trust each other.

1040
01:22:07,090 --> 01:22:11,440
If you come with us, 
we can't guarantee your safety.

1041
01:22:11,440 --> 01:22:15,840
But if it's Christa we're talking about, 
we might be able to do something for her.

1042
01:22:17,490 --> 01:22:21,490
Your petty life or Christa's future?

1043
01:22:22,690 --> 01:22:24,740
It's your decision.

1044
01:22:25,890 --> 01:22:28,410
<b><i>This world has no future?</i></b>

1045
01:22:28,410 --> 01:22:31,240
<b><i>What does that mean? 
And what is this "monkey"?</i></b>

1046
01:22:31,240 --> 01:22:33,240
<b><i>What is all this?</i></b>

1047
01:22:33,810 --> 01:22:35,640
Hey!

1048
01:22:35,640 --> 01:22:38,340
Hey, say it! Who's the enemy?

1049
01:22:40,410 --> 01:22:41,260
Ymir!

1050
01:22:49,090 --> 01:22:50,460
Who knows.

1051
01:22:51,410 --> 01:22:52,640
There you have it.

1052
01:22:53,790 --> 01:22:55,740
Too bad, Eren.

1053
01:23:04,490 --> 01:23:05,460
<b><i>Is that...</i></b>

1054
01:23:05,910 --> 01:23:08,310
<b><i>The Scout Regiment? Already?</i></b>

1055
01:23:10,560 --> 01:23:11,940
Dammit!

1056
01:23:16,510 --> 01:23:18,240
What's the deal, Reiner?

1057
01:23:18,240 --> 01:23:20,010
It isn't nighttime yet.

1058
01:23:20,010 --> 01:23:22,760
Nope. We're leaving now.

1059
01:23:22,760 --> 01:23:25,440
Eren, don't try to resist.

1060
01:23:26,740 --> 01:23:29,960
Come on, don't get violent with me.

1061
01:23:29,960 --> 01:23:34,960
Look at the shape that I'm in. 
Does it look like I can resist?

1062
01:23:34,960 --> 01:23:37,460
Please, gimme a break.

1063
01:23:45,910 --> 01:23:49,090
Die! Die! Die! Die! Die! Die!

1064
01:23:53,760 --> 01:23:56,240
I'll kill you! I'll slaughter you!

1065
01:23:56,960 --> 01:23:57,990
I'll kill you!

1066
01:23:57,990 --> 01:24:00,910
Hey. Why the change of plans?

1067
01:24:00,910 --> 01:24:04,600
Ymir, just before you turned back into a human,

1068
01:24:04,600 --> 01:24:07,190
do you remember who you ate?

1069
01:24:08,810 --> 01:24:12,140
Nope, not in the least.

1070
01:24:12,390 --> 01:24:15,460
But it <b><i>was</i></b> five years ago, so...

1071
01:24:16,260 --> 01:24:17,990
Was it a comrade of yours?

1072
01:24:22,310 --> 01:24:23,540
I see.

1073
01:24:23,840 --> 01:24:26,990
Sorry... for not even remembering.

1074
01:24:28,440 --> 01:24:31,040
I can't blame you for that.

1075
01:24:31,710 --> 01:24:34,240
It's the same for us, too.

1076
01:24:34,240 --> 01:24:35,410
I see...

1077
01:24:36,590 --> 01:24:38,540
Do you resent me for it?

1078
01:24:39,160 --> 01:24:40,900
I'm not sure...

1079
01:24:40,900 --> 01:24:43,210
I... don't know.

1080
01:24:43,990 --> 01:24:47,140
I doubt you actually wanted to eat anyone.

1081
01:24:47,140 --> 01:24:51,710
How long were you wandering around outside the walls?

1082
01:24:51,710 --> 01:24:54,290
About sixty years.

1083
01:24:54,290 --> 01:24:58,910
It felt like... I was trapped in an 
endless nightmare the entire time.

1084
01:25:05,640 --> 01:25:06,690
A flash!

1085
01:25:06,690 --> 01:25:09,810
I saw a light deep in the forest!

1086
01:25:10,060 --> 01:25:13,040
It's the light that appears 
when a Titan transforms!

1087
01:25:13,040 --> 01:25:14,510
We're just in time.

1088
01:25:14,510 --> 01:25:15,610
All troops, disperse!

1089
01:25:16,760 --> 01:25:19,260
Assume the enemy has already transformed!

1090
01:25:19,260 --> 01:25:21,260
Find Eren and recover him!

1091
01:25:31,310 --> 01:25:33,060
Not another Military Police!

1092
01:25:33,060 --> 01:25:34,610
Battle is not our objective!

1093
01:25:35,090 --> 01:25:38,630
Prioritize recovery and retreat!

1094
01:25:38,630 --> 01:25:40,440
Phil! Round up the horses!

1095
01:25:40,440 --> 01:25:41,690
Yes, sir!

1096
01:25:46,490 --> 01:25:49,390
Find the enemy and alert everyone to their location!

1097
01:25:49,390 --> 01:25:51,390
They must be trying to leave the forest!

1098
01:25:51,390 --> 01:25:52,240
Scatter!

1099
01:25:53,590 --> 01:25:54,360
<b><i>Eren...</i></b>

1100
01:25:54,360 --> 01:25:55,460
<b><i>Where are you?</i></b>

1101
01:26:00,610 --> 01:26:02,910
That was a Titan's roar!

1102
01:26:02,910 --> 01:26:04,160
It's coming from deeper in!

1103
01:26:08,910 --> 01:26:10,640
Of all the places!

1104
01:26:10,640 --> 01:26:12,110
Wait!

1105
01:26:13,490 --> 01:26:14,560
This is Ymir!

1106
01:26:14,910 --> 01:26:17,790
She's the one they took! 
This is her Titan form!

1107
01:26:17,790 --> 01:26:21,490
Where's Eren? 
And Reiner? Bertholdt?

1108
01:26:24,310 --> 01:26:25,960
That's Ymir?

1109
01:26:25,960 --> 01:26:28,410
Did she transform and fight them?

1110
01:26:28,410 --> 01:26:32,060
You got away from Reiner 
and Bertholdt? Where'd they go?

1111
01:26:32,060 --> 01:26:34,560
Please say something, Ymir!

1112
01:26:35,240 --> 01:26:36,760
Speak up already!

1113
01:26:37,160 --> 01:26:39,290
We don't have all day, ugly!

1114
01:26:42,290 --> 01:26:44,210
Something's strange.

1115
01:26:44,860 --> 01:26:46,360
Ymir!

1116
01:26:47,360 --> 01:26:49,910
Thank goodness! You're okay!

1117
01:26:56,960 --> 01:26:57,960
No way...

1118
01:26:57,960 --> 01:26:58,910
She just...

1119
01:26:59,240 --> 01:27:01,540
She just ate Christa!

1120
01:27:04,810 --> 01:27:07,340
Don't just stand there! After her!

1121
01:27:11,310 --> 01:27:13,960
She's too fast! We're losing her!

1122
01:27:13,960 --> 01:27:15,510
Why would Ymir do that?!

1123
01:27:15,510 --> 01:27:19,690
I can't be the only one who could have guessed it would turn out this way!

1124
01:27:19,690 --> 01:27:22,410
Yeah! She's clearly hostile to us now!

1125
01:27:22,410 --> 01:27:24,900
She's cooperating with Reiner and Bertholdt!

1126
01:27:24,900 --> 01:27:27,010
She lured us right in!

1127
01:27:28,610 --> 01:27:30,160
She's here, Reiner.

1128
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:01,890
All squads! Let the Titans chase you if you must!

1129
01:28:01,890 --> 01:28:03,790
Follow me!

1130
01:28:04,210 --> 01:28:05,310
Erwin...

1131
01:28:05,690 --> 01:28:09,860
You monster! 
You're using us as bait again?

1132
01:28:10,240 --> 01:28:12,340
They're taking Eren away!

1133
01:28:13,340 --> 01:28:14,840
Don't stop!

1134
01:28:15,090 --> 01:28:16,490
Follow them on horseback!

1135
01:28:24,990 --> 01:28:27,740
He's not fast enough to escape! We'll catch up!

1136
01:28:28,190 --> 01:28:32,290
This time, I won't hesitate. 
I'll kill them both, I swear!

1137
01:28:32,690 --> 01:28:36,540
No matter what it takes... I will!

1138
01:28:51,010 --> 01:28:51,960
Christa!

1139
01:28:59,740 --> 01:29:01,040
Ymir...

1140
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:10,190
Ymir!

1141
01:29:13,960 --> 01:29:15,210
Chrisâ€”

1142
01:29:16,510 --> 01:29:19,050
I mean, Historia.

1143
01:29:19,050 --> 01:29:22,860
Sorry... for suddenly... eating you.

1144
01:29:23,990 --> 01:29:27,210
I bet... you're mad at me.

1145
01:29:28,440 --> 01:29:29,490
Ymir...

1146
01:29:30,210 --> 01:29:33,060
What is this? 
What are you doing?

1147
01:29:33,060 --> 01:29:35,460
We came to rescue you and Ereâ€”

1148
01:29:35,460 --> 01:29:36,660
I don't need rescuing!

1149
01:29:37,460 --> 01:29:39,310
Just stay right there.

1150
01:29:39,710 --> 01:29:43,090
I'm following Reiner and Bertholdt now.

1151
01:29:43,090 --> 01:29:45,090
You, too. Come with me.

1152
01:29:46,360 --> 01:29:50,110
There's no future within the walls!

1153
01:29:52,410 --> 01:29:54,040
Listen, Historia.

1154
01:29:55,590 --> 01:29:59,260
Outside the walls isn't as bad as you think.

1155
01:29:59,260 --> 01:30:05,040
Nobody's gonna say it'd be 
better if you'd never been born.

1156
01:30:06,790 --> 01:30:09,960
Yeah, the Titans aren't gonna say that.

1157
01:30:09,960 --> 01:30:12,910
They'll be too busy trying to eat me!

1158
01:30:12,910 --> 01:30:16,140
Everyone has at least a fault or two!

1159
01:30:16,140 --> 01:30:19,310
If you can just overlook that, 
they're not so bad after all!

1160
01:30:19,310 --> 01:30:23,910
Ymir! Nothing you're saying or doing makes any sense!

1161
01:30:25,310 --> 01:30:29,710
Could it be... that Reiner and Bertholdt threatened you?

1162
01:30:32,710 --> 01:30:34,410
Am I right, Ymir?

1163
01:30:34,640 --> 01:30:38,290
I'll fight them with you, 
so let me out of your hand!

1164
01:30:38,690 --> 01:30:41,490
I don't care if there's something you can't tell me.

1165
01:30:41,490 --> 01:30:43,190
No matter what happens...

1166
01:30:43,190 --> 01:30:46,110
I'll always be on your side!

1167
01:31:26,960 --> 01:31:29,010
Reiner! Protect us!

1168
01:31:41,190 --> 01:31:44,060
<b><i>I knew it! I'll have to kill Ymir first!</i></b>

1169
01:31:44,940 --> 01:31:46,460
Wait, Mikasa!

1170
01:31:49,040 --> 01:31:50,560
Don't kill Ymir!

1171
01:31:50,640 --> 01:31:52,510
That all depends on Ymir!

1172
01:31:52,760 --> 01:31:56,150
What's it gonna be? 
I'll kill everyone that gets in my way.

1173
01:31:56,150 --> 01:31:56,990
Choose!

1174
01:31:56,990 --> 01:31:57,890
Wait!

1175
01:31:58,460 --> 01:32:01,760
Reiner and Bertholdt will kill Ymir too if she doesn't do what they say!

1176
01:32:01,760 --> 01:32:03,760
She doesn't have a choice!

1177
01:32:05,410 --> 01:32:08,210
There are only so many lives that I can value.

1178
01:32:08,640 --> 01:32:12,590
I decided who those people were six years ago.

1179
01:32:13,140 --> 01:32:16,740
So... you shouldn't try to ask for my pity.

1180
01:32:17,290 --> 01:32:22,410
Because right now, I'm all out of time 
and room in my heart to care.

1181
01:32:22,610 --> 01:32:26,250
Christa, it's either Eren or Ymir.

1182
01:32:26,250 --> 01:32:27,360
Which is it?

1183
01:32:27,860 --> 01:32:29,440
Will you get in my way, too?!

1184
01:32:30,690 --> 01:32:32,140
Stop, Ymir!

1185
01:32:32,140 --> 01:32:34,340
Don't fight back! You'll die!

1186
01:32:34,340 --> 01:32:35,510
Don't move!

1187
01:32:45,260 --> 01:32:46,260
Quit it, Eren!

1188
01:32:46,260 --> 01:32:48,790
Don't struggle!

1189
01:32:48,790 --> 01:32:51,310
Good luck with that, Bertholdt.

1190
01:32:51,310 --> 01:32:53,660
You know it's impossible to keep him down, right?

1191
01:32:53,660 --> 01:32:56,460
He's the most irritating guy there is!

1192
01:32:56,460 --> 01:32:59,910
I know better than anyone, 
'cause I hate him, too!

1193
01:32:59,910 --> 01:33:02,360
This is all some kind of lie, right?

1194
01:33:02,360 --> 01:33:06,410
Were you... really deceiving us this whole time?

1195
01:33:06,410 --> 01:33:08,110
That would be so cruel!

1196
01:33:08,110 --> 01:33:10,810
You guys! Please tell us it's all a lie!

1197
01:33:11,140 --> 01:33:13,040
Bertholdt, give him back!

1198
01:33:17,410 --> 01:33:21,510
Hey now, are you still trying to run away?

1199
01:33:21,510 --> 01:33:23,690
That's not gonna happen!

1200
01:33:23,690 --> 01:33:29,940
Didn't we sleep under the same roof as comrades 
through thick and thin for three years?

1201
01:33:29,940 --> 01:33:31,840
But you know, man...

1202
01:33:32,210 --> 01:33:39,260
I can't believe you could sleep at all right next all of your victims!

1203
01:33:39,260 --> 01:33:42,360
Remember when we talked about surviving this together?

1204
01:33:42,360 --> 01:33:46,560
And that we'd grow old, and someday we'd all go out for drinks together?

1205
01:33:46,560 --> 01:33:49,940
Was everything... all a lie?

1206
01:33:49,940 --> 01:33:50,910
Tell me!

1207
01:33:50,910 --> 01:33:52,710
You guys...

1208
01:33:52,710 --> 01:33:55,660
What were you thinking all this time?

1209
01:33:55,660 --> 01:33:57,990
None of that matters.

1210
01:33:57,990 --> 01:34:00,460
Just focus on taking their heads off.

1211
01:34:01,490 --> 01:34:03,290
They are enemies of humanity.

1212
01:34:03,290 --> 01:34:05,040
That's all we need to know.

1213
01:34:05,040 --> 01:34:08,340
If you hesitate for a second, 
we won't be able to get Eren back.

1214
01:34:07,110 --> 01:34:08,760
Do you think...

1215
01:34:09,090 --> 01:34:12,710
that anyone wants to kill people?

1216
01:34:16,940 --> 01:34:20,360
Who the hell would do this for fun?

1217
01:34:20,360 --> 01:34:23,140
Who'd <b><i>want</i></b> to do it?

1218
01:34:23,890 --> 01:34:29,340
We did something unforgivable. 
Something we should be killed for.

1219
01:34:29,340 --> 01:34:32,040
We can never take any of it back.

1220
01:34:34,040 --> 01:34:39,740
But... we just couldn't come to terms with our sins.

1221
01:34:39,740 --> 01:34:45,260
The only time we had some respite... 
was when we pretended to be soldiers.

1222
01:34:45,260 --> 01:34:46,740
That's not a lie!

1223
01:34:47,160 --> 01:34:52,840
Conny! Jean! It's true that 
we deceived you, but it's not all lies!

1224
01:34:52,840 --> 01:34:55,310
We really thought of you as comrades!

1225
01:34:57,340 --> 01:35:00,690
I know neither of us has the right to apologize.

1226
01:35:01,760 --> 01:35:04,640
But... someone...

1227
01:35:04,640 --> 01:35:05,710
Please...

1228
01:35:06,960 --> 01:35:10,160
Someone...

1229
01:35:10,160 --> 01:35:12,060
Please find us!

1230
01:35:17,710 --> 01:35:19,360
Bertholdt.

1231
01:35:20,210 --> 01:35:21,990
Give Eren back.

1232
01:35:22,690 --> 01:35:25,190
It's no use. I can't.

1233
01:35:26,310 --> 01:35:28,710
Someone has to do this.

1234
01:35:29,390 --> 01:35:33,960
Someone has to get blood on their hands!

1235
01:35:33,960 --> 01:35:35,960
You guys!

1236
01:35:35,960 --> 01:35:38,360
Get away from there!

1237
01:35:38,360 --> 01:35:40,010
This is unbelievable.

1238
01:35:40,290 --> 01:35:43,190
What are you thinking, Erwin?

1239
01:35:44,010 --> 01:35:47,160
He's brought Titans straight to us!

1240
01:35:56,410 --> 01:35:59,310
Everyone! Jump off right now!

1241
01:36:01,110 --> 01:36:02,560
Troops, disperse!

1242
01:36:02,560 --> 01:36:04,560
Get far away from the Titans!

1243
01:36:25,040 --> 01:36:26,640
Historia!

1244
01:36:35,590 --> 01:36:37,690
What's going on?

1245
01:36:37,690 --> 01:36:39,440
Is this hell?

1246
01:36:39,710 --> 01:36:41,940
No... but it will be!

1247
01:36:42,140 --> 01:36:43,940
All troops, attack!

1248
01:36:45,760 --> 01:36:49,940
The fate of humanity will be 
determined in this very moment!

1249
01:36:50,840 --> 01:36:56,910
Without Eren, there is no future 
for humanity in this world!

1250
01:36:56,910 --> 01:36:59,690
Take Eren back and retreat immediately!

1251
01:37:00,710 --> 01:37:03,460
Devote your hearts!

1252
01:37:05,240 --> 01:37:05,790
Mikasa!

1253
01:37:14,790 --> 01:37:18,460
<b><i>What's happening out there? 
What the hell's going on?</i></b>

1254
01:37:22,610 --> 01:37:24,340
<b><i>I can't move.</i></b>

1255
01:37:24,340 --> 01:37:28,690
<b><i>Unless I tear these Titans off me, it'll only get worse.</i></b>

1256
01:37:29,910 --> 01:37:31,590
<b><i>In that case...</i></b>

1257
01:37:31,590 --> 01:37:34,490
<b><i>Brace yourself, Bertholdt!</i></b>

1258
01:37:35,460 --> 01:37:36,860
<b><i>Just a little more.</i></b>

1259
01:37:37,390 --> 01:37:38,930
<b><i>We're almost there!</i></b>

1260
01:37:39,460 --> 01:37:40,910
It worked!

1261
01:37:40,910 --> 01:37:42,140
He moved his hands!

1262
01:37:42,140 --> 01:37:43,190
Now's our chance!

1263
01:37:43,190 --> 01:37:46,040
Hey, Mikasa?! Can't you see all those Titans?!

1264
01:37:46,560 --> 01:37:48,040
Advance!

1265
01:37:53,390 --> 01:37:56,740
Commander Erwin!

1266
01:37:57,440 --> 01:38:00,560
Advance!

1267
01:38:01,440 --> 01:38:03,690
Eren's just right in front of us!

1268
01:38:03,690 --> 01:38:05,740
Advance!

1269
01:38:39,810 --> 01:38:41,330
Mikasa!

1270
01:38:42,060 --> 01:38:43,910
You son of a bitch!

1271
01:38:43,910 --> 01:38:45,880
Let her go!

1272
01:38:52,240 --> 01:38:57,940
<b><i>Dammit. At this rate, everyone's gonna die all because I got captured.</i></b>

1273
01:38:57,940 --> 01:38:59,490
Bertholdt!

1274
01:39:00,760 --> 01:39:01,840
<b><i>Armin?!</i></b>

1275
01:39:04,860 --> 01:39:06,510
<b><i>What is it?</i></b>

1276
01:39:06,510 --> 01:39:08,960
<b><i>What is it that I have to abandon?</i></b>

1277
01:39:08,960 --> 01:39:10,560
<b><i>Is it my life?</i></b>

1278
01:39:12,190 --> 01:39:13,990
<b><i>Or something else?</i></b>

1279
01:39:28,040 --> 01:39:31,440
Are you sure about this, guys?

1280
01:39:31,440 --> 01:39:34,690
Leaving behind your comrade and returning home?

1281
01:39:38,240 --> 01:39:40,740
Are you abandoning Annie?

1282
01:39:40,740 --> 01:39:45,080
Because right now, she's far north, 
deep underground in Utopia District.

1283
01:39:45,500 --> 01:39:47,300
They're torturing her.

1284
01:39:49,210 --> 01:39:52,190
As soon as they heard her scream,

1285
01:39:52,190 --> 01:39:57,610
they realized that even if her 
wounds go away, her pain doesn't.

1286
01:39:58,540 --> 01:40:02,510
They're making sure she doesn't die.

1287
01:40:02,510 --> 01:40:07,420
And as we speak, 
they're not giving her body any rest.

1288
01:40:08,020 --> 01:40:11,680
They're putting her through a living hell!

1289
01:40:12,910 --> 01:40:14,880
You spawn of the devil!

1290
01:40:14,880 --> 01:40:16,880
I'll kill you all!

1291
01:40:37,050 --> 01:40:39,540
All troops, retreat!

1292
01:40:51,800 --> 01:40:53,090
Damn that Reiner!

1293
01:40:53,090 --> 01:40:55,600
He's throwing Titans at us!

1294
01:41:10,800 --> 01:41:12,710
Eren! Mikasa!

1295
01:41:17,450 --> 01:41:18,470
Eren...

1296
01:41:51,980 --> 01:41:52,960
Eren!

1297
01:41:57,220 --> 01:41:58,490
Mr. Hannes!

1298
01:42:05,200 --> 01:42:06,910
Talk about the chance of a lifetime.

1299
01:42:06,910 --> 01:42:08,660
Right, you two?

1300
01:42:09,290 --> 01:42:10,710
Just you watch!

1301
01:42:10,710 --> 01:42:15,180
I'm about to avenge your mother 
and butcher the shit out of this!

1302
01:42:19,510 --> 01:42:20,490
Mr. Hannes!

1303
01:42:21,110 --> 01:42:22,690
Give the old man backup!

1304
01:42:29,050 --> 01:42:33,140
Quit messing with us, you piece of shit!

1305
01:42:44,340 --> 01:42:45,470
I did it.

1306
01:42:46,050 --> 01:42:47,420
My first kill.

1307
01:42:53,750 --> 01:42:55,540
Are you all right, Christa?

1308
01:42:56,110 --> 01:42:58,400
Conny, that's wrong.

1309
01:42:58,400 --> 01:43:00,960
My name is Historia.

1310
01:43:01,560 --> 01:43:03,450
Hey, Ymir...

1311
01:43:04,290 --> 01:43:06,380
I don't know how to explain it,

1312
01:43:06,380 --> 01:43:09,380
but when I'm with you, 
no matter how screwed up it gets,

1313
01:43:10,400 --> 01:43:12,380
I'm not afraid!

1314
01:43:19,520 --> 01:43:20,270
Shit!

1315
01:43:30,310 --> 01:43:33,180
Don't, Mikasa! You're badly injured!

1316
01:43:35,360 --> 01:43:37,360
Untie my hands!

1317
01:43:37,360 --> 01:43:37,800
Hands?

1318
01:43:37,800 --> 01:43:39,270
Hurry up!

1319
01:43:39,270 --> 01:43:41,890
I've gotta be the one to do it!

1320
01:43:42,890 --> 01:43:45,420
Down here, ugly!

1321
01:43:47,340 --> 01:43:49,450
That one's... mine!

1322
01:43:49,450 --> 01:43:50,490
Eren!

1323
01:43:51,050 --> 01:43:53,960
Wait! We're trying to get you out of here!

1324
01:43:54,580 --> 01:43:56,910
I've got to settle this!

1325
01:43:56,910 --> 01:43:57,910
Just watch!

1326
01:44:13,470 --> 01:44:14,020
Commander.

1327
01:44:15,360 --> 01:44:17,070
The Armored Titan is coming!

1328
01:44:20,140 --> 01:44:20,940
Jean!

1329
01:44:26,050 --> 01:44:27,340
Jean!

1330
01:44:28,470 --> 01:44:30,020
Are you okay?

1331
01:44:30,020 --> 01:44:32,020
Hold it together!

1332
01:44:38,910 --> 01:44:40,340
Shit!

1333
01:44:41,870 --> 01:44:43,420
Why?!

1334
01:44:47,110 --> 01:44:47,850
Eren...

1335
01:45:13,140 --> 01:45:14,670
<b><i>Right now...</i></b>

1336
01:45:14,670 --> 01:45:17,160
<b><i>I have to become a Titan</i></b>

1337
01:45:19,470 --> 01:45:21,340
<b><i>or it's all for nothing!</i></b>

1338
01:46:04,290 --> 01:46:05,490
Eren...

1339
01:46:06,470 --> 01:46:07,820
Nothing's...

1340
01:46:08,310 --> 01:46:11,000
Nothing's changed at all!

1341
01:46:12,090 --> 01:46:15,160
You're still as fucking useless as you ever were!

1342
01:46:17,000 --> 01:46:19,180
Nothing's changed!

1343
01:46:29,870 --> 01:46:31,160
Mom...

1344
01:46:32,110 --> 01:46:34,140
I... can't...

1345
01:46:35,050 --> 01:46:38,760
I still... can't do anything at all.

1346
01:46:39,580 --> 01:46:40,780
Eren.

1347
01:46:48,200 --> 01:46:50,140
That's not true.

1348
01:47:10,020 --> 01:47:10,780
Eren.

1349
01:47:12,380 --> 01:47:13,450
Listen.

1350
01:47:15,200 --> 01:47:16,940
There's something I want to say.

1351
01:47:21,960 --> 01:47:27,200
Thank you... for always being with me.

1352
01:47:31,380 --> 01:47:38,360
Thank you... for teaching me 
how to live with purpose.

1353
01:47:44,220 --> 01:47:45,200
Thank you...

1354
01:47:48,910 --> 01:47:52,420
for wrapping this scarf around me.

1355
01:48:15,490 --> 01:48:17,180
I'll wrap that around you...

1356
01:48:17,870 --> 01:48:19,910
as many times as you want.

1357
01:48:22,180 --> 01:48:26,140
Now and forever... As much as you want!

1358
01:49:27,400 --> 01:49:29,820
Why are they...?

1359
01:49:30,490 --> 01:49:32,050
They're eating it?

1360
01:49:37,960 --> 01:49:40,420
Dunno what's going on, but now's our chance!

1361
01:49:40,420 --> 01:49:41,910
Let's hurry and run!

1362
01:49:43,200 --> 01:49:45,110
<b><i>So that's how it is...</i></b>

1363
01:49:45,110 --> 01:49:48,400
<b><i>That's why Reiner and Bertholdt 
were so desperate for Eren.</i></b>

1364
01:49:48,850 --> 01:49:51,880
<b><i>Which means, the world inside the walls...</i></b>

1365
01:49:52,310 --> 01:49:53,880
<b><i>has a future!</i></b>

1366
01:49:58,070 --> 01:50:00,090
<b><i>This is the worst...</i></b>

1367
01:50:00,090 --> 01:50:05,510
<b><i>How come the Coordinate has to fall into the hands of the worst person it possibly could?</i></b>

1368
01:50:05,510 --> 01:50:07,870
<b><i>We have to get it back.</i></b>

1369
01:50:07,870 --> 01:50:11,380
<b><i>There's no doubt about it. 
I'm absolutely certain.</i></b>

1370
01:50:11,380 --> 01:50:14,310
<b><i>The worst person in the world who could have that power...</i></b>

1371
01:50:14,800 --> 01:50:17,320
<b><i>is you, Eren!</i></b>

1372
01:50:18,380 --> 01:50:19,710
Get away from me!

1373
01:50:20,960 --> 01:50:23,960
You bastards! I'll kill you both!

1374
01:50:33,020 --> 01:50:35,420
<b><i>Crap! Bertholdt!</i></b>

1375
01:50:36,600 --> 01:50:38,490
<b><i>I can't protect Bertholdt like this!</i></b>

1376
01:50:38,690 --> 01:50:40,600
What? The Titans?

1377
01:50:40,600 --> 01:50:41,580
Eren!

1378
01:50:43,110 --> 01:50:44,000
Get on!

1379
01:50:44,000 --> 01:50:44,870
Armin!

1380
01:50:45,980 --> 01:50:46,780
Hurry!

1381
01:50:47,710 --> 01:50:49,850
Don't waste this opportunity.

1382
01:50:49,850 --> 01:50:51,540
Retreat!

1383
01:51:00,470 --> 01:51:02,000
Ymir!

1384
01:51:02,000 --> 01:51:05,140
Hey, ugly! Get off your butt! 
We're heading back!

1385
01:51:16,160 --> 01:51:18,420
I'm sorry.

1386
01:51:26,180 --> 01:51:28,270
Ymir? Where are you going?!

1387
01:51:28,270 --> 01:51:28,960
Leave her!

1388
01:51:28,960 --> 01:51:30,200
But Ymir isâ€”

1389
01:51:52,420 --> 01:51:57,780
<b><i>At that time, we didn't know 
what Ymir's actions meant</i></b>

1390
01:51:58,760 --> 01:52:02,650
<b><i>But after that, the Armored Titan 
didn't pursue us any further.</i></b>

1391
01:52:18,540 --> 01:52:20,090
Ymir...

1392
01:52:20,090 --> 01:52:22,510
Why did you come with us?

1393
01:52:22,780 --> 01:52:24,910
Well...

1394
01:52:26,270 --> 01:52:28,890
If you hadn't come to destroy this wall,

1395
01:52:29,270 --> 01:52:33,120
I would've never woken up from that nightmare.

1396
01:52:33,540 --> 01:52:35,660
All I'm doing

1397
01:52:36,290 --> 01:52:39,750
is returning what I borrowed back then.

1398
01:52:41,540 --> 01:52:43,110
Besides...

1399
01:52:45,800 --> 01:52:50,780
Being a goddess doesn't feel so bad, you know.

1400
01:52:56,780 --> 01:52:58,980
This is just our theory.

1401
01:52:59,870 --> 01:53:05,240
The Titans were ignoring us and heading for Reiner.

1402
01:53:07,710 --> 01:53:11,090
We think it was because of you.

1403
01:53:12,200 --> 01:53:14,340
It's a tough spot to be in, Eren.

1404
01:53:15,180 --> 01:53:17,420
Whether all those people died for nothing or not,

1405
01:53:18,380 --> 01:53:20,620
it all depends on you.

1406
01:53:24,980 --> 01:53:28,050
Yeah, you're absolutely right.

1407
01:53:29,870 --> 01:53:31,600
I've gotta do this.

1408
01:53:31,600 --> 01:53:33,360
I'll control the Titans.

1409
01:53:33,910 --> 01:53:35,600
I'll seal Wall Maria.

1410
01:53:36,160 --> 01:53:39,480
I'll find Reiner and Bertholdt and make them pay.

1411
01:53:40,250 --> 01:53:44,440
That's what I've gotta do 
to atone for all those lives lost.

1412
01:53:46,940 --> 01:53:47,820
Say again?

1413
01:53:48,110 --> 01:53:53,200
The Titans responsible for this incident... 
were the residents of Ragako Village?

1414
01:53:54,420 --> 01:53:58,290
In other words, the true identity of Titans...

1415
01:53:58,490 --> 01:54:00,450
...is humans?

1416
01:54:02,020 --> 01:54:03,850
So... you're telling me...

1417
01:54:04,870 --> 01:54:08,010
that I've been flying all over the place

1418
01:54:08,800 --> 01:54:12,000
killing humans this whole time?

1419
01:54:12,000 --> 01:54:13,270
Is that right?

1420
01:54:14,200 --> 01:54:17,400
We have no solid proof yet.

1421
01:54:21,270 --> 01:54:22,250
Erwin.

1422
01:54:25,400 --> 01:54:30,360
The hell... are you smiling about?

1423
01:54:35,020 --> 01:54:36,800
It's nothing.

1424
01:54:38,110 --> 01:54:39,910
It's just...

1425
01:54:40,110 --> 01:54:44,910
with this, we're one step closer to the truth.

1426
01:54:46,220 --> 01:54:48,600
Just one step, huh?

1427
01:54:48,600 --> 01:54:52,340
We'll run out of people 
before we learn the truth.

1428
01:54:52,340 --> 01:54:54,050
It's not worth the cost.

1429
01:54:54,940 --> 01:54:57,070
But it is a step towards the truth.

1430
01:54:58,270 --> 01:55:01,180
One day, we'll finally break it down.

1431
01:55:02,220 --> 01:55:04,360
These walls hiding the truth...

1432
01:55:05,960 --> 01:55:07,180
...will fall.

1433
01:55:10,050 --> 01:55:13,490
<b>Wouldn't it be nice to take a walk</b>

1434
01:55:13,490 --> 01:55:16,800
<b>on some pure white sand,</b>

1435
01:55:16,800 --> 01:55:20,180
<b>gaze at the horizon</b>

1436
01:55:20,180 --> 01:55:23,500
<b>without living in fear?</b>

1437
01:55:23,500 --> 01:55:27,400
<b>Wouldn't it be sweet to watch the sun curve</b>

1438
01:55:27,400 --> 01:55:30,800
<b>down mid the waves</b>

1439
01:55:30,800 --> 01:55:34,090
<b>and taste the ocean spray</b>

1440
01:55:34,090 --> 01:55:38,820
<b>and realize we've been living</b>

1441
01:55:38,820 --> 01:55:42,000
<b>as slaves?</b>

1442
01:55:42,000 --> 01:55:45,270
<b>We've got to learn to get back, get back</b>

1443
01:55:45,270 --> 01:55:48,670
<b>but is it worth the price of our soul?</b>

1444
01:55:48,670 --> 01:55:52,510
<b>You know you had to kill her, kill her!</b>

1445
01:55:52,510 --> 01:55:55,760
<b>Oh my dirty hands, it never fades</b>

1446
01:55:55,760 --> 01:55:58,690
<b>And if we get out, get out</b>

1447
01:55:58,690 --> 01:56:01,980
<b>I'll think about the price of our soul</b>

1448
01:56:01,980 --> 01:56:05,310
<b>We've got to learn to live free, live free</b>

1449
01:56:05,310 --> 01:56:09,290
<b>We'll live a life without barricades</b>

1450
01:56:59,470 --> 01:57:04,140
<b>How long I haven't seen the light shine
through in my life?</b>

1451
01:57:04,140 --> 01:57:06,400
<b>Lost everything, family</b>

1452
01:57:06,400 --> 01:57:08,560
<b>Confusion on the way</b>

1453
01:57:08,560 --> 01:57:13,690
<b>Someone tries to talk to me
and signpost the righteous road</b>

1454
01:57:13,690 --> 01:57:15,910
<b>My animal inside</b>

1455
01:57:15,910 --> 01:57:19,280
<b>can now be tamed to go over</b>

1456
01:57:19,280 --> 01:57:21,310
<b>the wall</b>

1457
01:57:21,310 --> 01:57:23,690
<b>We've got to learn to get back, get back</b>

1458
01:57:23,690 --> 01:57:25,940
<b>but is it worth the price of our soul?</b>

1459
01:57:25,940 --> 01:57:28,560
<b>You know you had to kill her, kill her!</b>

1460
01:57:28,560 --> 01:57:30,870
<b>Oh my dirty hands, it never fades</b>

1461
01:57:30,870 --> 01:57:32,870
<b>And if we get out, get out</b>

1462
01:57:32,870 --> 01:57:35,090
<b>I'll think about the price of our soul</b>

1463
01:57:35,090 --> 01:57:37,340
<b>We've got to learn to live free, live free</b>

1464
01:57:37,340 --> 01:57:40,340
<b>We'll live a life without barricades</b>

1465
01:58:20,270 --> 01:58:26,070
Sasha, if you sneak some of this food out, 
I'll have Captain Levi turn you into mincemeat.

1466
01:58:26,070 --> 01:58:28,850
I won't. Probably...

1467
01:58:28,850 --> 01:58:30,140
Say what?

1468
01:58:30,140 --> 01:58:33,600
Hey! Did you guys clean your shoes before you came in?

1469
01:58:34,670 --> 01:58:38,530
No, we didn't. How could we clean our shoes while carrying all this?

1470
01:58:38,530 --> 01:58:42,740
What do you think Captain Levi would have to say about that attitude?

1471
01:58:42,740 --> 01:58:45,980
If I hadn't tucked in your sheets this morninâ€”

1472
01:58:45,980 --> 01:58:49,340
Quit nagging! Who are you, my mom!?

1473
01:58:49,340 --> 01:58:50,780
We're back.

1474
01:58:50,780 --> 01:58:53,160
Wait, why were you chopping firewood?

1475
01:58:53,160 --> 01:58:54,690
My body's getting dull.

1476
01:58:54,690 --> 01:58:57,710
You got grabbed by a Titan! 
You shouldn't be moving yet!

1477
01:58:57,710 --> 01:59:01,820
I tried to stop her, but she wouldn't listen. 
She was even doing sit-ups earlier!

1478
01:59:02,220 --> 01:59:04,160
You were peeping on her, you scoundrel?

1479
01:59:04,160 --> 01:59:04,680
Huh?

1480
01:59:04,680 --> 01:59:07,740
Mikasa, you're not a wild animal!

1481
01:59:05,510 --> 01:59:07,740
What part of that sounded like peeping to you!?

1482
01:59:07,740 --> 01:59:11,940
It kinda feels like we're back in the Cadet Corps.

1483
01:59:11,940 --> 01:59:13,420
Yeah...

1484
01:59:13,420 --> 01:59:17,650
But why were we all picked for the new Squad Levi?

1485
01:59:18,070 --> 01:59:21,540
Isn't protecting Eren and Historia too important to leave up to us?

1486
01:59:21,540 --> 01:59:23,690
Because we're talented, I assume.

1487
01:59:25,020 --> 01:59:28,110
What did you just put in your bag?

1488
01:59:28,110 --> 01:59:30,510
Nothing bread-related.

1489
01:59:30,510 --> 01:59:32,410
Why you!

1490
01:59:32,410 --> 01:59:33,450
Put it back.

1491
01:59:33,450 --> 01:59:37,340
Hey, focus! We gotta finish cleaning 
before the Captain gets back!

1492
01:59:37,340 --> 01:59:39,070
Put back the bread.

1493
01:59:39,070 --> 01:59:41,340
Why are you all fighting?

1494
01:59:39,070 --> 01:59:41,340
You just never learn, do you?

1495
01:59:41,340 --> 01:59:43,420
We can't afford to waste food!

1496
01:59:43,420 --> 01:59:46,710
Cut the crap, Potato Girl!

1497
01:59:54,400 --> 01:59:57,740
I <b><i>know</i></b> I gave you enough time.

1498
02:00:12,690 --> 02:00:14,100
Ackermann?

1499
02:00:14,600 --> 02:00:16,510
Is that his last name?

1500
02:00:17,310 --> 02:00:21,090
I lived with him for a while when I was a kid.
